{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b5b460d23b13a3f0","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t{\n2\t  \"branchName\": \"iotahub/phase-1\",\n3\t  \"userStories\": [\n4\t    {\n5\t      \"id\": \"STORY-setup-001\",\n6\t      \"title\": \"Initialize repository workspace git config and project root files\",\n7\t      \"description\": \"Create the root repository workspace structure including git initialization, comprehensive .gitignore for Node and Next.js, README.md, .editorconfig, and root package.json. Defines the foundational workspace environment for subsequent scaffolding stories.\",\n8\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n9\t        \"Repository root contains initialized `.git` directory and clean working tree.\",\n10\t        \"`.gitignore` exists covering `node_modules`, `.next`, `.env`, and build artifacts.\",\n11\t        \"`.editorconfig` specifies 2-space indentation, UTF-8 encoding, and LF line endings.\",\n12\t        \"`README.md` documents repository layout, setup prerequisites, and development scripts.\",\n13\t        \"Root `package.json` initializes project name as `spotify` with private package status.\"\n14\t      ],\n15\t      \"priority\": 0,\n16\t      \"passes\": false,\n17\t      \"dependsOn\": [],\n18\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n19\t      \"effort\": \"small\",\n20\t      \"model\": \"haiku\"\n21\t    },\n22\t    {\n23\t      \"id\": \"STORY-setup-002\",\n24\t      \"title\": \"Scaffold Next.js 14 fullstack monolith project baseline\",\n25\t      \"description\": \"Scaffold a Next.js 14 App Router project with TypeScript 5.x support in the root directory. Configures strict TypeScript compiler options, App Router directory layout (`/app`), and basic page/layout entrypoints.\",\n26\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n27\t        \"Next.js 14 App Router project initialized with TypeScript 5.x configuration in root directory.\",\n28\t        \"`tsconfig.json` enforces `strict: true`, `target: ES2022`, and path aliases `@/*` pointing to `./src/*`.\",\n29\t        \"`app/layout.tsx` and `app/page.tsx` exist as minimal functional React Server Components.\",\n30\t        \"Running `npm run build` completes with exit code 0 and produces optimized standalone build output.\",\n31\t        \"Running `npm run dev` boots Next.js development server on `http://localhost:3000` without runtime errors.\"\n32\t      ],\n33\t      \"priority\": 1,\n34\t      \"passes\": false,\n35\t      \"dependsOn\": [\n36\t        \"STORY-setup-001\"\n37\t      ],\n38\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n39\t      \"effort\": \"small\",\n40\t      \"model\": \"haiku\"\n41\t    },\n42\t    {\n43\t      \"id\": \"STORY-setup-003\",\n44\t      \"title\": \"Install core dependencies and configure Tailwind CSS with shadcn UI\",\n45\t      \"description\": \"Install Tailwind CSS 3.4+, Radix UI primitives, shadcn/ui integration, lucide-react icons, and music-metadata. Sets up dark-mode first HSL design tokens, responsive grid defaults down to 375px viewports, and utility styling classes.\",\n46\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n47\t        \"Dependencies `@radix-ui/react-slot`, `clsx`, `tailwind-merge`, `lucide-react`, `music-metadata` installed in `package.json`.\",\n48\t        \"`tailwind.config.js` configures dark mode, HSL color tokens, typography scales, and content paths for `/src`.\",\n49\t        \"`src/app/globals.css` defines CSS custom properties for dark-first HSL palette and WCAG AA contrast levels.\",\n50\t        \"`components.json` configured for shadcn/ui primitive component auto-generation.\",\n51\t        \"Unit test verifies helper utility `cn()` correctly merges Tailwind CSS classes.\"\n52\t      ],\n53\t      \"priority\": 2,\n54\t      \"passes\": false,\n55\t      \"dependsOn\": [\n56\t        \"STORY-setup-002\"\n57\t      ],\n58\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n59\t      \"effort\": \"small\",\n60\t      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n61\t    },\n62\t    {\n63\t      \"id\": \"STORY-setup-004\",\n64\t      \"title\": \"Implement MongoDB database schema and Prisma ORM models\",\n65\t      \"description\": \"Configure Prisma ORM v5.x with MongoDB provider. Implement all 8 core canonical models (User, ArtistProfile, Track, Playlist, PlaylistTrack, Like, Follow, Report, AuditLog) and required enums, compound unique indexes, and relational attributes.\",\n66\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n67\t        \"`prisma/schema.prisma` created with MongoDB provider and 8 canonical models matching exact field specifications.\",\n68\t        \"Enums `UserRole`, `AccountStatus`, `TrackStatus`, `Genre`, `ReportReason`, `ReportStatus`, and `AuditAction` defined.\",\n69\t        \"Compound unique indexes `@unique([playlistId, position])`, `@unique([playlistId, trackId])`, `@unique([userId, trackId])`, `@unique([followerId, artistProfileId])` configured.\",\n70\t        \"`npx prisma validate` succeeds and `npx prisma generate` outputs type-safe PrismaClient SDK.\",\n71\t        \"Unit test instantiates PrismaClient and validates all model typings compile without TypeScript errors.\"\n72\t      ],\n73\t      \"priority\": 3,\n74\t      \"passes\": false,\n75\t      \"dependsOn\": [\n76\t        \"STORY-setup-003\"\n77\t      ],\n78\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n79\t      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n80\t      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n81\t    },\n82\t    {\n83\t      \"id\": \"STORY-setup-005\",\n84\t      \"title\": \"Implement StorageService interface abstraction for S3 signed URLs\",\n85\t      \"description\": \"Implement the vendor-agnostic `StorageService` interface wrapping `@aws-sdk/client-s3`. Provides methods for file upload, object deletion, and generating 60-minute presigned PUT upload URLs and 15-minute presigned GET stream delivery URLs.\",\n86\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n87\t        \"`StorageService` interface implemented in `src/lib/storage/storage.service.ts` with `uploadObject`, `deleteObject`, `generateSignedUrl`.\",\n88\t        \"`S3StorageService` implementation handles AWS S3 / Cloudflare R2 compatible endpoint configurations.\",\n89\t        \"`generateSignedUrl` enforces 3600-second TTL cap for `getObject` streaming requests.\",\n90\t        \"Unit tests mock S3 client and verify correct presigned URL generation and parameter passing for `putObject` and `getObject`.\",\n91\t        \"Integration test validates audio upload size constraint validation helper caps files at 50MB.\"\n92\t      ],\n93\t      \"priority\": 4,\n94\t      \"passes\": false,\n95\t      \"dependsOn\": [\n96\t        \"STORY-setup-004\"\n97\t      ],\n98\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n99\t      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n100\t      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n101\t    },\n102\t    {\n103\t      \"id\": \"STORY-setup-006\",\n104\t      \"title\": \"Implement standardized REST API response wrappers and validation middleware\",\n105\t      \"description\": \"Implement standard API JSON success and error outer envelopes, request ID tracing, UTC ISO-8601 timestamping, and a Zod schema validation middleware returning 422 Unprocessable Entity details arrays.\",\n106\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n107\t        \"Success helper `apiSuccessResponse(data, meta)` constructs payload with `success: true`, `data`, UTC timestamp, and `requestId`.\",\n108\t        \"Error helper `apiErrorResponse(code, message, details)` constructs payload with `success: false`, `error` code, and optional `details` array.\",\n109\t        \"Validation middleware `validateBody(schema)` validates Zod schema and returns HTTP 422 with `ValidationErrorDetail` format on failure.\",\n110\t        \"Passwords and sensitive credentials are sanitized and excluded from error payload outputs and log traces.\",\n111\t        \"Integration tests cover `apiSuccessResponse`, `apiErrorResponse`, and Zod validation failure scenarios for HTTP status codes 400, 422, and 500.\"\n112\t      ],\n113\t      \"priority\": 5,\n114\t      \"passes\": false,\n115\t      \"dependsOn\": [\n116\t        \"STORY-setup-005\"\n117\t      ],\n118\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n119\t      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n120\t      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n121\t    },\n122\t    {\n123\t      \"id\": \"STORY-setup-007\",\n124\t      \"title\": \"Implement JWT authentication middleware and admin RBAC route guards\",\n125\t      \"description\": \"Build server-side authentication middleware handling 7-day HTTP-only cookies containing JWT session tokens. Implement bcrypt cost-12 password hashing helpers and strict server-side RBAC middleware for `/api/v1/admin/*` and `/admin/*` routes.\",\n126\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n127\t        \"`hashPassword` and `comparePassword` utilities wrap `bcryptjs` using cost factor 12.\",\n128\t        \"`generateToken` and `verifyToken` helpers handle 7-day JWT stateless session payloads.\",\n129\t        \"Next.js `middleware.ts` intercepts `/admin/*` and `/api/v1/admin/*` routes, enforcing `ADMIN` user role server-side.\",\n130\t        \"Unauthenticated requests to protected paths return HTTP 401 `UNAUTHENTICATED`, non-admin requests return HTTP 403 `FORBIDDEN_INSUFFICIENT_ROLE`.\",\n131\t        \"Integration tests verify JWT session extraction from HTTP-only cookies and RBAC route protection for Listener vs Admin roles.\"\n132\t      ],\n133\t      \"priority\": 6,\n134\t      \"passes\": false,\n135\t      \"dependsOn\": [\n136\t        \"STORY-setup-006\"\n137\t      ],\n138\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n139\t      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n140\t      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n141\t    },\n142\t    {\n143\t      \"id\": \"STORY-setup-008\",\n144\t      \"title\": \"Implement limit-offset pagination contracts and response helpers\",\n145\t      \"description\": \"Create standard pagination parser and formatter utilities for REST collection endpoints. Enforces 1-indexed page numbers, default 20-item limits, 100-item maximum caps, and paginated API response JSON structures.\",\n146\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n147\t        \"`parsePaginationParams(url)` parses `page` (default 1) and `limit` (default 20, max 100).\",\n148\t        \"`apiPaginatedResponse(data, total, page, limit)` returns JSON envelope containing `data[]`, `pagination` object (`total`, `page`, `limit`, `totalPages`, `hasNextPage`, `hasPreviousPage`), and `meta`.\",\n149\t        \"`limit` values exceeding 100 are automatically clamped to 100.\",\n150\t        \"Unit tests in `src/lib/api/pagination.test.ts` test default fallback, maximum clamping, and total page calculation math.\",\n151\t        \"Integration test verifies query parameter parsing against a dummy collection route.\"\n152\t      ],\n153\t      \"priority\": 7,\n154\t      \"passes\": false,\n155\t      \"dependsOn\": [\n156\t        \"STORY-setup-007\"\n157\t      ],\n158\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n159\t      \"effort\": \"small\",\n160\t      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n161\t    },\n162\t    {\n163\t      \"id\": \"STORY-setup-009\",\n164\t      \"title\": \"Configure Vitest unit integration test runner and Playwright E2E setup\",\n165\t      \"description\": \"Configure Vitest for server/service unit testing and Playwright for frontend E2E browser testing. Includes test scripts in `package.json`, environment setup, and baseline passing test suites.\",\n166\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n167\t        \"Vitest configured with `@testing-library/react` and Node.js environment in `vitest.config.ts`.\",\n168\t        \"Playwright configured in `playwright.config.ts` targeting standard web viewports (desktop and 375px mobile).\",\n169\t        \"`npm run test` executes Vitest unit/integration tests with exit code 0.\",\n170\t        \"`npm run test:e2e` executes Playwright specs against running dev server with exit code 0.\",\n171\t        \"Sample unit test `src/lib/sample.test.ts` and sample E2E spec `e2e/home.spec.ts` pass cleanly.\"\n172\t      ],\n173\t      \"priority\": 8,\n174\t      \"passes\": false,\n175\t      \"dependsOn\": [\n176\t        \"STORY-setup-008\"\n177\t      ],\n178\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n179\t      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n180\t      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n181\t    },\n182\t    {\n183\t      \"id\": \"STORY-setup-010\",\n184\t      \"title\": \"Configure environment variable schema template and GitHub Actions CI workflow\",\n185\t      \"description\": \"Create `.env.example` defining all required runtime secrets and setup a GitHub Actions CI pipeline running linting, TypeScript compilation, Prisma schema validation, Vitest unit tests, and Playwright E2E suites.\",\n186\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n187\t        \"`.env.example` created listing `DATABASE_URL`, `JWT_SECRET`, `AWS_REGION`, `AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID`, `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY`, `S3_BUCKET_NAME`, `S3_ENDPOINT`.\",\n188\t        \"`src/lib/env.ts` implements Zod parsing for process.env at server startup.\",\n189\t        \"`.github/workflows/ci.yml` created with steps: checkout, node setup, install dependencies, lint, typecheck, prisma validate, vitest run, playwright test.\",\n190\t        \"Build fails in CI if TypeScript compilation contains errors or test coverage target is breached.\",\n191\t        \"Manual execution of CI workflow steps locally succeeds cleanly.\"\n192\t      ],\n193\t      \"priority\": 9,\n194\t      \"passes\": false,\n195\t      \"dependsOn\": [\n196\t        \"STORY-setup-009\"\n197\t      ],\n198\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n199\t      \"effort\": \"small\",\n200\t      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n201\t    },\n202\t    {\n203\t      \"id\": \"STORY-security-001\",\n204\t      \"title\": \"Implement Bcrypt Password Hashing and Payload Sanitization Utility\",\n205\t      \"description\": \"Create a backend security service using bcrypt with cost factor 12 and 16-byte random salt to hash user passwords prior to storage in MongoDB. Include automatic sanitization functions to strip passwordHash from Prisma database queries and API response payloads.\",\n206\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n207\t        \"Hashing passwords using bcrypt generates a valid salt and hash using cost factor 12.\",\n208\t        \"Verifying a raw password against the stored hash returns true for correct input and false for invalid input.\",\n209\t        \"Sanitization helper function strips passwordHash from User model objects before JSON serialization.\",\n210\t        \"Prisma query select wrappers omit passwordHash from returned fields unless explicitly selected.\",\n211\t        \"Password hashes are never written to standard log streams or error stack trace outputs per sec-024 sensitive data security rules.\",\n212\t        \"Unit tests in tests/unit/security/password.test.ts verify hashing, cost factor 12 execution time (~250ms), verification logic, and payload sanitization.\"\n213\t      ],\n214\t      \"priority\": 10,\n215\t      \"passes\": false,\n216\t      \"dependsOn\": [\n217\t        \"STORY-setup-004\"\n218\t      ],\n219\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n220\t      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n221\t      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n222\t    },\n223\t    {\n224\t      \"id\": \"STORY-security-002\",\n225\t      \"title\": \"Implement Session JWT Token Service and Secure Cookie Serialization\",\n226\t      \"description\": \"Develop a stateless JWT session token management service that signs and verifies claims including userId, role, and optional artistProfileId using HMAC-SHA256. Configure HTTP-only, SameSite=Strict, Secure cookie serialization with a 7-day expiration under __Host-indie_session.\",\n227\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n228\t        \"JWT token generation includes userId, role ('LISTENER'|'ARTIST'|'ADMIN'), optional artistProfileId, iat, and exp claims signed with JWT_SECRET.\",\n229\t        \"Session cookie serialization sets __Host-indie_session with HttpOnly: true, Secure: true, SameSite: Strict, Path: /, and Max-Age: 604800 (7 days).\",\n230\t        \"Expired or tampered JWT signatures fail verification and throw a structured session invalidation error.\",\n231\t        \"All timestamp claims (iat, exp) adhere to UTC ISO-8601 / Unix epoch standards in UTC per constraint 0.\",\n232\t        \"Unit tests in tests/unit/security/session.test.ts cover token creation, claim validation, signature tampering, expiration checks, and cookie header formatting.\"\n233\t      ],\n234\t      \"priority\": 11,\n235\t      \"passes\": false,\n236\t      \"dependsOn\": [\n237\t        \"STORY-setup-007\"\n238\t      ],\n239\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n240\t      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n241\t      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n242\t    },\n243\t    {\n244\t      \"id\": \"STORY-security-003\",\n245\t      \"title\": \"Implement Next.js Edge Middleware for Server-Side Route Guarding\",\n246\t      \"description\": \"Build Next.js Edge Middleware in middleware.ts to intercept protected routes /admin/*, /api/v1/admin/*, /api/v1/artist/*, /api/v1/playlists/*, and /api/v1/reports/*. Verify session cookies, validate role hierarchy, and inject decoded identity claims into request headers.\",\n247\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n248\t        \"Unauthenticated requests targeting protected routes return HTTP status 401 Unauthorized.\",\n249\t        \"Authenticated requests lacking required roles (e.g. Listener accessing /admin/*) return HTTP status 403 Forbidden per constraint 3.\",\n250\t        \"Valid requests propagate decoded session claims in custom request headers x-user-id, x-user-role, and x-artist-profile-id to downstream handlers.\",\n251\t        \"Public routes (such as guest search and track streaming) bypass middleware role checks per DEC-005.\",\n252\t        \"Unit tests cover middleware claim parsing and route matcher logic.\",\n253\t        \"Integration tests verify HTTP 401, 403, and header injection behavior for protected API routes.\"\n254\t      ],\n255\t      \"priority\": 12,\n256\t      \"passes\": false,\n257\t      \"dependsOn\": [\n258\t        \"STORY-setup-007\",\n259\t        \"STORY-security-002\"\n260\t      ],\n261\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n262\t      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n263\t      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n264\t    },\n265\t    {\n266\t      \"id\": \"STORY-security-004\",\n267\t      \"title\": \"Implement Resource Ownership Verification Helpers and IDOR Protection\",\n268\t      \"description\": \"Implement reusable backend resource authorization functions to enforce Insecure Direct Object Reference (IDOR) protection in REST API route handlers. Ensure users can only modify or delete their own Track and Playlist records unless they hold the Admin role.\",\n269\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n270\t        \"Track ownership check confirms Track.artistProfileId equals caller's artistProfileId or caller holds ADMIN role.\",\n271\t        \"Playlist ownership check confirms Playlist.userId equals caller's userId or caller holds ADMIN role.\",\n272\t        \"Failed ownership checks abort execution and return HTTP 403 Forbidden with code ERR_RESOURCE_OWNERSHIP_DENIED and detailed resource info.\",\n273\t        \"Admin role overrides ownership restrictions across all Track and Playlist update and delete handlers.\",\n274\t        \"Integration tests assert HTTP 403 response structure when an unauthorized user attempts to edit another user's playlist or track.\"\n275\t      ],\n276\t      \"priority\": 13,\n277\t      \"passes\": false,\n278\t      \"dependsOn\": [\n279\t        \"STORY-security-001\",\n280\t        \"STORY-security-002\"\n281\t      ],\n282\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n283\t      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n284\t      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n285\t    },\n286\t    {\n287\t      \"id\": \"STORY-security-005\",\n288\t      \"title\": \"Implement Higher-Order withAuth and withRole API Handler Wrappers\",\n289\t      \"description\": \"Create higher-order functions withAuth and withRole to wrap Next.js API handlers, extract session claims, build an immutable AuthContext, and handle authentication error responses uniformly.\",\n290\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n291\t        \"withAuth extracts claims from request headers injected by middleware or direct cookie verification and constructs immutable AuthContext.\",\n292\t        \"withRole verifies that AuthContext.user.role matches one of the specified allowed roles for the route.\",\n293\t        \"Token invalidation or expiry caught inside the wrapper returns HTTP 401 Unauthorized with standardized envelope error code ERR_UNAUTHORIZED.\",\n294\t        \"Unit tests in tests/unit/security/wrappers.test.ts verify AuthContext injection and role boundary validation.\",\n295\t        \"Integration tests confirm 401 error envelope format when calling wrapped endpoints without valid session headers.\"\n296\t      ],\n297\t      \"priority\": 14,\n298\t      \"passes\": false,\n299\t      \"dependsOn\": [\n300\t        \"STORY-security-002\",\n301\t        \"STORY-setup-006\"\n302\t      ],\n303\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n304\t      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n305\t      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n306\t    },\n307\t    {\n308\t      \"id\": \"STORY-storage-001\",\n309\t      \"title\": \"Implement Unified StorageProvider Interface for S3 and Cloudflare R2\",\n310\t      \"description\": \"Build the StorageProvider abstraction layer utilizing AWS SDK v3 to support Amazon S3 and Cloudflare R2 object storage backends. Dynamically select provider implementation based on the STORAGE_PROVIDER environment variable.\",\n311\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n312\t        \"StorageProvider interface exposes generatePresignedUploadUrl, generatePresignedDownloadUrl, deleteObject, and getObjectMetadata.\",\n313\t        \"System initializes AWS S3 or Cloudflare R2 client according to STORAGE_PROVIDER ('s3' or 'r2') environment configuration per DEC-008.\",\n314\t        \"Presigned upload URLs generate valid S3/R2 PUT targets with specified TTL.\",\n315\t        \"Presigned download URLs generate access-controlled GET targets with specified TTL.\",\n316\t        \"Unit tests mock AWS SDK calls to test presigned URL creation, metadata reading, and object deletion.\",\n317\t        \"Integration tests against mock S3 storage verify presigned upload token generation and metadata retrieval.\"\n318\t      ],\n319\t      \"priority\": 15,\n320\t      \"passes\": false,\n321\t      \"dependsOn\": [\n322\t        \"STORY-setup-005\"\n323\t      ],\n324\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n325\t      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n326\t      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n327\t    },\n328\t    {\n329\t      \"id\": \"STORY-storage-002\",\n330\t      \"title\": \"Implement Upload Intent API Endpoint with Media Validation\",\n331\t      \"description\": \"Create backend endpoint POST /api/v1/storage/upload-intent to validate file metadata against audio and image size/MIME rules before returning direct-to-storage presigned upload URLs.\",\n332\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n333\t        \"Endpoint accepts fileType ('audio'|'image'), fileName, fileSizeBytes, and mimeType.\",\n334\t        \"Audio uploads are restricted to MP3 (audio/mpeg) and WAV (audio/wav) up to 50MB (52,428,800 bytes) per constraint 1.\",\n335\t        \"Cover image uploads are restricted to JPEG, PNG, and WebP up to 10MB (10,485,760 bytes).\",\n336\t        \"Invalid file formats or sizes exceeding limits return HTTP 422 Unprocessable Entity with details before presigning.\",\n337\t        \"Valid requests return HTTP 200 OK with a 60-minute presigned PUT URL and deterministic object key (audio/{artistId}/{trackId}_{uuid}.{ext} or images/{artistId}/{imageId}_{uuid}.webp).\",\n338\t        \"Integration test verifies POST /api/v1/storage/upload-intent with valid and invalid audio payloads.\"\n339\t      ],\n340\t      \"priority\": 16,\n341\t      \"passes\": false,\n342\t      \"dependsOn\": [\n343\t        \"STORY-storage-001\",\n344\t        \"STORY-security-005\"\n345\t      ],\n346\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n347\t      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n348\t      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n349\t    },\n350\t    {\n351\t      \"id\": \"STORY-storage-003\",\n352\t      \"title\": \"Implement Presigned Playback Stream URL Endpoint and Byte Range Headers\",\n353\t      \"description\": \"Create backend endpoint GET /api/v1/tracks/:id/stream to issue short-lived GET presigned playback URLs (15-minute TTL) with HTTP byte-range request header support for low-latency streaming.\",\n354\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n355\t        \"Request generates a presigned GET URL with a 900-second (15-minute) expiration for track playback per DEC-008.\",\n356\t        \"Allows unauthenticated guest access for public track streaming per DEC-005.\",\n357\t        \"Emits HTTP response headers Accept-Ranges: bytes and Cache-Control: private, max-age=900.\",\n358\t        \"Supports HTTP 206 Partial Content range responses with Content-Range: bytes <start>-<end>/<total> to meet SLA of under 2 seconds audio playback start per sec-024.\",\n359\t        \"Unit tests verify stream URL generation and expiry configuration.\",\n360\t        \"Integration test calls GET /api/v1/tracks/:id/stream and verifies response headers and presigned stream URL payload.\"\n361\t      ],\n362\t      \"priority\": 17,\n363\t      \"passes\": false,\n364\t      \"dependsOn\": [\n365\t        \"STORY-storage-001\",\n366\t        \"STORY-setup-004\"\n367\t      ],\n368\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n369\t      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n370\t      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n371\t    },\n372\t    {\n373\t      \"id\": \"STORY-storage-004\",\n374\t      \"title\": \"Implement Frontend Direct-to-Storage Upload Hook and Upload Component\",\n375\t      \"description\": \"Build React hook useDirectUpload and UI component FileUploadProgress to request presigned upload URLs from the storage API and execute client-side direct binary uploads to S3/R2 with progress indicators.\",\n376\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n377\t        \"useDirectUpload hook manages request flow: POST /upload-intent, direct S3/R2 PUT binary transfer, progress state, and completion.\",\n378\t        \"UI displays real-time progress bar, transfer percentage, and error notifications adhering to design tokens.\",\n379\t        \"Pre-upload client validation checks file size (max 50MB audio) and MIME format before network requests.\",\n380\t        \"Upload controls and progress indicators satisfy WCAG 2.1 AA accessibility keyboard and screen reader standards per constraint 5.\",\n381\t        \"Responsive layout scales down gracefully to 375px mobile viewports per sec-026.\",\n382\t        \"Unit tests in tests/unit/components/upload.test.tsx test hook states and upload validation.\",\n383\t        \"Playwright E2E spec in e2e/tests/upload-flow.spec.ts verifies selecting an audio file, observing progress, and completing direct upload.\"\n384\t      ],\n385\t      \"priority\": 18,\n386\t      \"passes\": false,\n387\t      \"dependsOn\": [\n388\t        \"STORY-storage-002\",\n389\t        \"STORY-setup-003\"\n390\t      ],\n391\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n392\t      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n393\t      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n394\t    },\n395\t    {\n396\t      \"id\": \"STORY-auth-001\",\n397\t      \"title\": \"Implement User Registration API Endpoint and Payload Validation\",\n398\t      \"description\": \"Build POST /api/v1/auth/register API endpoint to validate registration payloads, enforce email normalization and uniqueness, create User records with bcrypt password hashes, and return a 7-day session cookie.\",\n399\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n400\t        \"Accepts { email, password, displayName }, normalizes email to lowercase, and validates password strength (min 8 chars, 1 uppercase, 1 lowercase, 1 digit).\",\n401\t        \"Returns HTTP 409 Conflict with code AUTH_EMAIL_EXISTS if email is already registered.\",\n402\t        \"Hashes password using bcrypt cost 12 and creates User record with role LISTENER per DEC-004.\",\n403\t        \"Sets __Host-indie_session HTTP-only, SameSite=Strict cookie with 7-day TTL and returns HTTP 201 Created with sanitized user object.\",\n404\t        \"Timestamps (createdAt) are stored and returned in UTC ISO-8601 format per constraint 0.\",\n405\t        \"Passwords are sanitized out of response payloads and never logged per constraint 4 and sec-024 rules.\",\n406\t        \"Integration test asserts POST /api/v1/auth/register creates user, sets session cookie, and returns sanitized envelope.\"\n407\t      ],\n408\t      \"priority\": 19,\n409\t      \"passes\": false,\n410\t      \"dependsOn\": [\n411\t        \"STORY-security-001\",\n412\t        \"STORY-security-002\",\n413\t        \"STORY-setup-004\"\n414\t      ],\n415\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n416\t      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n417\t      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n418\t    },\n419\t    {\n420\t      \"id\": \"STORY-auth-002\",\n421\t      \"title\": \"Implement User Login API Endpoint with Rate Limiting\",\n422\t      \"description\": \"Build POST /api/v1/auth/login endpoint to authenticate registered users via email and password, issue session cookies, and enforce a 5-attempt per 15-minute rate limit policy per IP address.\",\n423\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n424\t        \"Validates email and password, returning HTTP 200 OK and setting the 7-day __Host-indie_session cookie upon successful match.\",\n425\t        \"Returns HTTP 401 Unauthorized with code INVALID_CREDENTIALS for non-existent emails or incorrect passwords.\",\n426\t        \"Enforces rate limiting: exceeding 5 failed login attempts in 15 minutes per IP triggers HTTP 429 Too Many Requests with code RATE_LIMIT_EXCEEDED per sec-025.\",\n427\t        \"Password inputs and failure attempts do not output plaintext credentials to application loggers per constraint 4.\",\n428\t        \"Integration test verifies successful login cookie issuance, 401 error envelope on invalid credentials, and 429 rate limit triggering after 5 failed attempts.\"\n429\t      ],\n430\t      \"priority\": 20,\n431\t      \"passes\": false,\n432\t      \"dependsOn\": [\n433\t        \"STORY-security-001\",\n434\t        \"STORY-security-002\"\n435\t      ],\n436\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n437\t      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n438\t      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n439\t    },\n440\t    {\n441\t      \"id\": \"STORY-auth-003\",\n442\t      \"title\": \"Implement Password Reset and Credential Management APIs\",\n443\t      \"description\": \"Implement backend endpoints POST /api/v1/auth/forgot-password, POST /api/v1/auth/reset-password, and PATCH /api/v1/auth/password for self-service password recovery and authenticated credential updates.\",\n444\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n445\t        \"POST /api/v1/auth/forgot-password generates a 60-minute reset token stored as a hash in DB and returns a uniform HTTP 200 OK response to prevent email enumeration.\",\n446\t        \"POST /api/v1/auth/reset-password validates reset token, updates bcrypt password hash, invalidates used token, and revokes active session cookies.\",\n447\t        \"PATCH /api/v1/auth/password verifies caller's currentPassword, updates to newPassword, and regenerates the session token.\",\n448\t        \"Password reset tokens and updated hashes use UTC ISO-8601 expiration timestamps per constraint 0.\",\n449\t        \"Integration tests cover forgot password uniform response, reset password execution, token expiry rejection, and credential update logic.\"\n450\t      ],\n451\t      \"priority\": 21,\n452\t      \"passes\": false,\n453\t      \"dependsOn\": [\n454\t        \"STORY-auth-001\",\n455\t        \"STORY-security-001\"\n456\t      ],\n457\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n458\t      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n459\t      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n460\t    },\n461\t    {\n462\t      \"id\": \"STORY-auth-004\",\n463\t      \"title\": \"Implement Log Sanitization and Password Field Protection Middleware\",\n464\t      \"description\": \"Build global logging middleware to intercept incoming request bodies on auth routes and sanitize sensitive credential fields (password, oldPassword, newPassword) before passing logs to central monitoring.\",\n465\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n466\t        \"Middleware inspects incoming payload bodies on /api/v1/auth/* routes and replaces sensitive keys with [REDACTED].\",\n467\t        \"Structured application error logs strip password fields from stack traces and error details.\",\n468\t        \"Data in transit is enforced over TLS 1.3 encrypted connections per sec-025.\",\n469\t        \"Unit tests in tests/unit/middleware/sanitizer.test.ts verify payload redaction across various nested JSON structures.\"\n470\t      ],\n471\t      \"priority\": 22,\n472\t      \"passes\": false,\n473\t      \"dependsOn\": [\n474\t        \"STORY-setup-006\",\n475\t        \"STORY-security-001\"\n476\t      ],\n477\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n478\t      \"effort\": \"small\",\n479\t      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n480\t    },\n481\t    {\n482\t      \"id\": \"STORY-auth-005\",\n483\t      \"title\": \"Implement Guest Session Migration Service\",\n484\t      \"description\": \"Create client and backend helper functions to migrate temporary in-memory/localStorage guest playlist drafts and queue state into permanent Playlist records upon user registration or sign-in.\",\n485\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n486\t        \"Guest session state reader extracts local draft playlist tracks from client storage post-registration.\",\n487\t        \"Client issues POST /api/v1/playlists with guest playlist data to create permanent database records linked to the new User.id.\",\n488\t        \"Active audio streaming player state is preserved continuously across registration without resetting playback per DEC-005.\",\n489\t        \"Unit tests verify guest state extraction and payload formatting.\",\n490\t        \"Integration test validates converting a guest playlist payload into a persisted Playlist entity.\"\n491\t      ],\n492\t      \"priority\": 23,\n493\t      \"passes\": false,\n494\t      \"dependsOn\": [\n495\t        \"STORY-auth-001\",\n496\t        \"STORY-setup-004\"\n497\t      ],\n498\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n499\t      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n500\t      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n501\t    },\n502\t    {\n503\t      \"id\": \"STORY-auth-006\",\n504\t      \"title\": \"Implement Frontend Account Registration Page and Interactive Form\",\n505\t      \"description\": \"Build Next.js user registration page /register featuring Zod schema client-side validation, password strength meter, show/hide password toggle, accessible loading states, and responsive shadcn layout.\",\n506\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n507\t        \"Renders /register page using dark-mode design system tokens, responsive grid layouts down to 375px mobile viewports per sec-026.\",\n508\t        \"Input fields for email, password, and displayName validate on blur and submit using Zod schema rules.\",\n509\t        \"Password input features an interactive visibility toggle button (masked vs unmasked) and real-time password strength meter.\",\n510\t        \"API submission displays active loading spinner on submit button, disables re-clicks with aria-disabled=\\\"true\\\".\",\n511\t        \"Server errors (such as AUTH_EMAIL_EXISTS) render in an accessible alert banner at the top of the form with focus moved to the first invalid field per WCAG 2.1 AA (constraint 5).\",\n512\t        \"Unit tests verify form validation rules and component state transitions.\",\n513\t        \"Playwright E2E spec e2e/tests/register.spec.ts covers successful registration, duplicate email handling, and validation error display.\"\n514\t      ],\n515\t      \"priority\": 24,\n516\t      \"passes\": false,\n517\t      \"dependsOn\": [\n518\t        \"STORY-auth-001\",\n519\t        \"STORY-setup-003\"\n520\t      ],\n521\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n522\t      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n523\t      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n524\t    },\n525\t    {\n526\t      \"id\": \"STORY-auth-007\",\n527\t      \"title\": \"Implement Frontend Login Page and Form Component\",\n528\t      \"description\": \"Build Next.js user login page /login with Zod validation, error callout banners, password visibility toggle, guest session migration trigger, and seamless redirect after authentication.\",\n529\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n530\t        \"Renders /login page using design tokens and responsive layout down to 375px mobile viewport per sec-026.\",\n531\t        \"Form validates email and password inputs, displaying inline feedback on invalid submission.\",\n532\t        \"Successful login triggers guest session state migration if guest playlist items exist in local storage per DEC-005.\",\n533\t        \"Password field includes show/hide visibility toggle and accessible label associations complying with WCAG 2.1 AA per constraint 5.\",\n534\t        \"Server authentication errors (such as INVALID_CREDENTIALS or RATE_LIMIT_EXCEEDED) display in an accessible alert callout banner.\",\n535\t        \"Unit tests verify login form states and submit event handling.\",\n536\t        \"Playwright E2E spec e2e/tests/login.spec.ts tests valid login flow, invalid credentials error, and guest migration trigger.\"\n537\t      ],\n538\t      \"priority\": 25,\n539\t      \"passes\": false,\n540\t      \"dependsOn\": [\n541\t        \"STORY-auth-002\",\n542\t        \"STORY-auth-005\",\n543\t        \"STORY-setup-003\"\n544\t      ],\n545\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n546\t      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n547\t      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n548\t    },\n549\t    {\n550\t      \"id\": \"STORY-auth-008\",\n551\t      \"title\": \"Implement Frontend Password Recovery Pages\",\n552\t      \"description\": \"Build Next.js UI pages /forgot-password and /reset-password allowing users to request password reset links and submit new credentials with real-time feedback and accessibility.\",\n553\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n554\t        \"/forgot-password page accepts email and presents a confirmation message regardless of email existence to prevent account enumeration.\",\n555\t        \"/reset-password page extracts reset token from URL query params and validates new password against strength rules before submitting.\",\n556\t        \"Visual feedback banners notify user of successful password reset and provide a link to sign in.\",\n557\t        \"Form controls adhere to WCAG 2.1 AA keyboard navigation and screen reader standards per constraint 5.\",\n558\t        \"Unit tests verify form schema validation and token state handling.\",\n559\t        \"Playwright E2E spec e2e/tests/password-reset.spec.ts verifies full password recovery user flow from forgot-password submission to reset-password update.\"\n560\t      ],\n561\t      \"priority\": 26,\n562\t      \"passes\": false,\n563\t      \"dependsOn\": [\n564\t        \"STORY-auth-003\",\n565\t        \"STORY-setup-003\"\n566\t      ],\n567\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n568\t      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n569\t      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n570\t    },\n571\t    {\n572\t      \"id\": \"STORY-role-001\",\n573\t      \"title\": \"Implement Listener to Artist Role Upgrade API Endpoint\",\n574\t      \"description\": \"Create the POST /api/v1/users/me/upgrade-to-artist API endpoint allowing registered Listener users to upgrade to an Artist role. Executes an atomic transaction to append the ARTIST role flag to User.roles, provision a linked ArtistProfile model, and return an updated JWT session payload. Preserves existing user favorites, playlists, and follow relationships without requiring re-registration.\",\n575\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n576\t        \"POST /api/v1/users/me/upgrade-to-artist appends 'ARTIST' to User.roles while preserving 'LISTENER' privileges.\",\n577\t        \"Provisions an ArtistProfile record with userId, stageName (defaulting to User.name if omitted), bio, genreTags, and initial followerCount=0, trackCount=0.\",\n578\t        \"Returns HTTP 200 OK with the updated User object, new ArtistProfile, and a fresh JWT containing revised role claims.\",\n579\t        \"Timestamps in the response payload are formatted in UTC ISO-8601 per constraint [0].\",\n580\t        \"Unit tests in src/services/role.test.ts verify atomic role update and default stageName fallback logic.\",\n581\t        \"Integration test calls POST /api/v1/users/me/upgrade-to-artist with valid payload and asserts HTTP 200 plus correct database state.\"\n582\t      ],\n583\t      \"priority\": 27,\n584\t      \"passes\": false,\n585\t      \"dependsOn\": [\n586\t        \"STORY-setup-004\",\n587\t        \"STORY-security-002\"\n588\t      ],\n589\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n590\t      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n591\t      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n592\t    },\n593\t    {\n594\t      \"id\": \"STORY-role-002\",\n595\t      \"title\": \"Implement Verification Email Generation and Dispatch Service\",\n596\t      \"description\": \"Build the backend service and API endpoint POST /api/v1/auth/verify-email/request to generate cryptographically secure email verification tokens. Generates a 64-character hex token via crypto.randomBytes(32), stores a SHA-256 digest in the database with a 24-hour expiration window, invalidates previous active tokens, and dispatches a single-use verification link via email.\",\n597\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n598\t        \"POST /api/v1/auth/verify-email/request generates a 64-character random token and persists its SHA-256 digest with expiresAt set 24 hours in the future.\",\n599\t        \"Invalidates any existing active verification token records for the requesting user prior to creating a new token.\",\n600\t        \"Returns HTTP 202 Accepted with a confirmation message and expiresInSeconds=86400.\",\n601\t        \"Applies rate limiting on POST /api/v1/auth/verify-email/request per cross-cutting security policy sec-025.\",\n602\t        \"Unit tests in src/services/emailVerification.test.ts cover token generation, SHA-256 hashing, and prior token invalidation.\",\n603\t        \"Integration test calls POST /api/v1/auth/verify-email/request for an authenticated user and asserts HTTP 202 status and DB record.\"\n604\t      ],\n605\t      \"priority\": 28,\n606\t      \"passes\": false,\n607\t      \"dependsOn\": [\n608\t        \"STORY-setup-004\",\n609\t        \"STORY-security-002\"\n610\t      ],\n611\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n612\t      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n613\t      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n614\t    },\n615\t    {\n616\t      \"id\": \"STORY-role-003\",\n617\t      \"title\": \"Implement Email Verification Token Confirmation and Status APIs\",\n618\t      \"description\": \"Implement POST /api/v1/auth/verify-email/confirm to validate incoming raw tokens against SHA-256 database digests and GET /api/v1/users/me/verification-status to retrieve email verification status. Validates token freshness (expiresAt > current_time), sets User.emailVerified to true with a UTC ISO-8601 timestamp, deletes used token records, and returns explicit status data.\",\n619\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n620\t        \"POST /api/v1/auth/verify-email/confirm hashes incoming raw token with SHA-256 and matches against active database records.\",\n621\t        \"If token is valid and unexpired, updates User.emailVerified to true, sets emailVerifiedAt to UTC ISO-8601 timestamp, and deletes the token record.\",\n622\t        \"If token is invalid or expired, returns HTTP 400 Bad Request with error code INVALID_VERIFICATION_TOKEN.\",\n623\t        \"GET /api/v1/users/me/verification-status returns HTTP 200 OK with emailVerified, canUpload boolean, and roles array.\",\n624\t        \"Unit tests in src/services/emailVerificationConfirm.test.ts cover valid token processing, expired token rejection, and invalid digest matching.\",\n625\t        \"Integration test calls POST /api/v1/auth/verify-email/confirm with valid and invalid tokens and verifies exact HTTP responses.\"\n626\t      ],\n627\t      \"priority\": 29,\n628\t      \"passes\": false,\n629\t      \"dependsOn\": [\n630\t        \"STORY-role-002\"\n631\t      ],\n632\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n633\t      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n634\t      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n635\t    },\n636\t    {\n637\t      \"id\": \"STORY-role-004\",\n638\t      \"title\": \"Implement Email Verification Gating Middleware for Track Uploads\",\n639\t      \"description\": \"Implement the requireVerifiedEmail middleware enforcing DEC-004, which restricts track upload execution exclusively to users with verified email addresses. Intercepts request flows targeting POST /api/v1/tracks and POST /api/v1/tracks/upload-intent, rejecting unverified users with HTTP 403 Forbidden without affecting streaming, search, or playlist actions.\",\n640\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n641\t        \"requireVerifiedEmail middleware checks User.emailVerified property on authenticated request contexts.\",\n642\t        \"If User.emailVerified is false, rejects request immediately with HTTP 403 Forbidden and code EMAIL_NOT_VERIFIED containing resendUrl.\",\n643\t        \"Allows verified users with ARTIST role to proceed through upload execution handlers.\",\n644\t        \"Explicitly leaves streaming, playback, search, following, and playlist endpoints ungated per DEC-004 and DEC-005.\",\n645\t        \"Unit tests in src/middleware/requireVerifiedEmail.test.ts verify passthrough for verified users and rejection for unverified accounts.\",\n646\t        \"Integration test verifies that POST /api/v1/tracks returns 403 when invoked by an unverified account.\"\n647\t      ],\n648\t      \"priority\": 30,\n649\t      \"passes\": false,\n650\t      \"dependsOn\": [\n651\t        \"STORY-role-003\",\n652\t        \"STORY-security-005\"\n653\t      ],\n654\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n655\t      \"effort\": \"small\",\n656\t      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n657\t    },\n658\t    {\n659\t      \"id\": \"STORY-role-005\",\n660\t      \"title\": \"Implement Frontend Artist Upgrade Form and Settings Section\",\n661\t      \"description\": \"Build the frontend artist role upgrade modal and account settings form component allowing Listeners to transition into Artists. Collects stageName, bio, and genreTags with client-side validation, submits data to POST /api/v1/users/me/upgrade-to-artist, updates global authentication state, and displays creator onboarding guidance.\",\n662\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n663\t        \"Renders form fields for stageName (1-50 chars), bio (max 500 chars), and genreTags (1-5 tags select) within account settings.\",\n664\t        \"Complies with WCAG 2.1 AA keyboard accessibility standards and visible focus highlights per constraint [5].\",\n665\t        \"On successful submission, updates session context with ARTIST role and redirects or shows artist dashboard link without requiring re-login.\",\n666\t        \"Displays error alert banner if validation or API failure occurs.\",\n667\t        \"Unit tests in src/components/ArtistUpgradeForm.test.tsx verify field validation, submission handling, and accessibility attributes.\",\n668\t        \"Playwright spec in e2e/tests/artist-upgrade.spec.ts covers filling out the upgrade form, submitting, and verifying updated role state.\"\n669\t      ],\n670\t      \"priority\": 31,\n671\t      \"passes\": false,\n672\t      \"dependsOn\": [\n673\t        \"STORY-role-001\",\n674\t        \"STORY-setup-003\"\n675\t      ],\n676\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n677\t      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n678\t      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n679\t    },\n680\t    {\n681\t      \"id\": \"STORY-role-006\",\n682\t      \"title\": \"Implement Frontend Email Verification Confirmation Page and Notification Banner\",\n683\t      \"description\": \"Construct the email verification landing page (/verify-email) and sticky notification banner for unverified creator accounts. Reads the token query parameter on mount, invokes POST /api/v1/auth/verify-email/confirm, renders success or error confirmation states, and provides a one-click resend button triggering POST /api/v1/auth/verify-email/request.\",\n684\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n685\t        \"Landing page at /verify-email extracts token parameter and automatically triggers confirmation API request on load.\",\n686\t        \"Renders success message with button to return to artist dashboard upon HTTP 200 OK response.\",\n687\t        \"Renders error alert with explicit message and 'Resend Verification Email' action button when token is invalid or expired.\",\n688\t        \"Displays a persistent banner in creator views when User.emailVerified is false, explaining upload gating per DEC-004.\",\n689\t        \"Unit tests in src/pages/VerifyEmail.test.tsx verify token extraction, API invocation states, and error handling UI.\",\n690\t        \"Playwright spec in e2e/tests/email-verification.spec.ts tests visiting /verify-email with valid and expired tokens.\"\n691\t      ],\n692\t      \"priority\": 32,\n693\t      \"passes\": false,\n694\t      \"dependsOn\": [\n695\t        \"STORY-role-003\",\n696\t        \"STORY-setup-003\"\n697\t      ],\n698\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n699\t      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n700\t      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n701\t    },\n702\t    {\n703\t      \"id\": \"STORY-profile-001\",\n704\t      \"title\": \"Implement Get Public Artist Profile API with Aggregated Metrics\",\n705\t      \"description\": \"Develop the GET /api/v1/artists/:artistId endpoint to fetch public artist profiles, live tracks, and real-time aggregated metrics. Aggregates total plays across live tracks, total likes count, and followers count, and includes top 5 popular tracks ordered descending by play count.\",\n706\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n707\t        \"GET /api/v1/artists/:artistId returns public profile details (displayName, bio, avatarUrl, headerImageUrl, socialLinks, isVerified).\",\n708\t        \"Calculates and returns aggregated stats: totalPlays (sum of live track playCounts), totalLikes (count of likes across tracks), and followerCount.\",\n709\t        \"Returns top 5 tracks owned by artist with status 'LIVE' ordered descending by playCount.\",\n710\t        \"Accessible to unauthenticated guest users per DEC-005, returning isFollowing boolean if authenticated request context exists.\",\n711\t        \"Unit tests in src/services/artistProfile.test.ts cover aggregation calculations, popular track selection, and guest request handling.\",\n712\t        \"Integration test calls GET /api/v1/artists/:artistId and verifies response schema, stats accuracy, and 200 HTTP status.\"\n713\t      ],\n714\t      \"priority\": 33,\n715\t      \"passes\": false,\n716\t      \"dependsOn\": [\n717\t        \"STORY-role-001\",\n718\t        \"STORY-setup-008\"\n719\t      ],\n720\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n721\t      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n722\t      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n723\t    },\n724\t    {\n725\t      \"id\": \"STORY-profile-002\",\n726\t      \"title\": \"Implement Update Artist Profile API Endpoint and Payload Validation\",\n727\t      \"description\": \"Create the PATCH /api/v1/artist-profile API endpoint allowing creators with the ARTIST role to update branding metadata. Validates payload fields against strict schema constraints (displayName 1-50 chars, bio max 500 chars, socialLinks max 5 HTTPS entries) and returns 422 error codes upon validation failure.\",\n728\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n729\t        \"PATCH /api/v1/artist-profile enforces ARTIST role authorization requirement.\",\n730\t        \"Validates displayName (1-50 chars, trimmed), bio (max 500 chars), and socialLinks (max 5 items, valid HTTPS URLs with matching platforms).\",\n731\t        \"Returns HTTP 422 Unprocessable Entity with codes INVALID_DISPLAY_NAME, BIO_TOO_LONG, or INVALID_SOCIAL_LINKS upon invalid payloads.\",\n732\t        \"Returns HTTP 200 OK with the updated ArtistProfile payload upon successful modification.\",\n733\t        \"Unit tests in src/validators/artistProfile.test.ts verify field validation rules and error payload generation.\",\n734\t        \"Integration test executes PATCH /api/v1/artist-profile with valid and invalid payloads and verifies responses.\"\n735\t      ],\n736\t      \"priority\": 34,\n737\t      \"passes\": false,\n738\t      \"dependsOn\": [\n739\t        \"STORY-role-001\",\n740\t        \"STORY-security-005\"\n741\t      ],\n742\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n743\t      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n744\t      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n745\t    },\n746\t    {\n747\t      \"id\": \"STORY-profile-003\",\n748\t      \"title\": \"Implement Avatar and Header Image Upload Endpoints for Artist Profiles\",\n749\t      \"description\": \"Build the POST /api/v1/artist-profile/avatar and POST /api/v1/artist-profile/header endpoints for multipart image uploads. Validates image file sizes (max 5MB), MIME types (JPEG, PNG, WebP), uploads assets to cloud storage via StorageProvider, and updates avatarUrl or headerImageUrl on the ArtistProfile model.\",\n750\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n751\t        \"POST /api/v1/artist-profile/avatar and /header endpoints accept multipart image file uploads up to 5MB.\",\n752\t        \"Validates MIME type to ensure file is image/jpeg, image/png, or image/webp, returning 422 INVALID_AVATAR_URL or INVALID_HEADER_URL on mismatch.\",\n753\t        \"Uploads processed images to storage provider and updates target ArtistProfile record with HTTPS asset URL.\",\n754\t        \"Requires ARTIST role authorization and returns updated profile payload in JSON envelope.\",\n755\t        \"Unit tests in src/services/profileImageUpload.test.ts cover file type validation, size checking, and storage provider invocation.\",\n756\t        \"Integration test posts image files to avatar/header endpoints and asserts HTTP 200 status and updated profile fields.\"\n757\t      ],\n758\t      \"priority\": 35,\n759\t      \"passes\": false,\n760\t      \"dependsOn\": [\n761\t        \"STORY-profile-002\",\n762\t        \"STORY-storage-001\"\n763\t      ],\n764\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n765\t      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n766\t      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n767\t    },\n768\t    {\n769\t      \"id\": \"STORY-profile-004\",\n770\t      \"title\": \"Implement Listener Public Profile API Endpoint\",\n771\t      \"description\": \"Develop the GET /api/v1/users/:userId endpoint for fetching public listener profiles. Returns basic user metadata (username, avatar, registration year), public playlists grid data (where isPublic=true), and a list of followed artists.\",\n772\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n773\t        \"GET /api/v1/users/:userId returns public user info including username, avatarUrl, and createdAt registration year.\",\n774\t        \"Includes public playlists list created by the user where isPublic is true, formatted with title, trackCount, and cover mosaic.\",\n775\t        \"Includes array of followed ArtistProfile summary objects.\",\n776\t        \"Accessible to both authenticated users and unauthenticated guests per DEC-005.\",\n777\t        \"Unit tests in src/services/listenerProfile.test.ts verify filtering of private playlists and proper profile serialization.\",\n778\t        \"Integration test calls GET /api/v1/users/:userId and asserts HTTP 200 response with correct public data.\"\n779\t      ],\n780\t      \"priority\": 36,\n781\t      \"passes\": false,\n782\t      \"dependsOn\": [\n783\t        \"STORY-setup-008\"\n784\t      ],\n785\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n786\t      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n787\t      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n788\t    },\n789\t    {\n790\t      \"id\": \"STORY-profile-005\",\n791\t      \"title\": \"Implement Account Suspension and Banned Status Profile Isolation Filter\",\n792\t      \"description\": \"Implement global security filtering to soft-hide suspended or banned profiles and content per DEC-003. Ensures GET /api/v1/artists/:artistId and GET /api/v1/users/:userId return HTTP 404 Not Found when target accounts are suspended or banned, filtering them out of public searches and catalog queries.\",\n793\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n794\t        \"If a target User record has status 'SUSPENDED' or 'BANNED', profile endpoints GET /api/v1/artists/:artistId and GET /api/v1/users/:userId return HTTP 404 NOT_FOUND.\",\n795\t        \"Filters out suspended or banned artists and their tracks from search indices and catalog listing queries.\",\n796\t        \"Maintains database record integrity without hard-deleting underlying tracks or profiles per DEC-003.\",\n797\t        \"Unit tests in src/middleware/statusIsolation.test.ts cover profile 404 responses for suspended and banned user states.\",\n798\t        \"Integration test verifies that querying a suspended artist's profile route returns a standardized 404 error envelope.\"\n799\t      ],\n800\t      \"priority\": 37,\n801\t      \"passes\": false,\n802\t      \"dependsOn\": [\n803\t        \"STORY-profile-001\",\n804\t        \"STORY-profile-004\"\n805\t      ],\n806\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n807\t      \"effort\": \"small\",\n808\t      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n809\t    },\n810\t    {\n811\t      \"id\": \"STORY-profile-006\",\n812\t      \"title\": \"Implement Frontend Public Artist Profile Page and Discography View\",\n813\t      \"description\": \"Construct the public artist profile view (/artists/[artistId]) displaying branding header, metrics bar, popular tracks section, and paginated discography. Renders dynamic header banner, circular avatar, follower count, follow/unfollow toggle, popular tracks table (top 5), and full track catalog with sorting options.\",\n814\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n815\t        \"Renders header banner image (16:9 ratio with default gradient fallback), 128x128px circular avatar, displayName, bio, and social links.\",\n816\t        \"Displays metrics bar showing formatted total plays, total likes, and follower counts using compact notation (e.g. 1.2K).\",\n817\t        \"Renders Popular Tracks section (up to 5 items) with inline play buttons, genre badges, duration, and play/like counts.\",\n818\t        \"Displays full published track catalog with Release Date (default) and Title sort controls, supporting infinite scroll loading.\",\n819\t        \"Includes interactive Follow/Unfollow button that toggles state for logged-in users and prompts login modal for guests.\",\n820\t        \"Unit tests in src/pages/ArtistProfileView.test.tsx cover header rendering, stats formatting, track list sorting, and follow button interaction.\",\n821\t        \"Playwright spec in e2e/tests/artist-profile.spec.ts verifies visiting /artists/[artistId], interacting with play triggers, and sorting discography.\"\n822\t      ],\n823\t      \"priority\": 38,\n824\t      \"passes\": false,\n825\t      \"dependsOn\": [\n826\t        \"STORY-profile-001\",\n827\t        \"STORY-setup-003\"\n828\t      ],\n829\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n830\t      \"effort\": \"high\",\n831\t      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n832\t    },\n833\t    {\n834\t      \"id\": \"STORY-profile-007\",\n835\t      \"title\": \"Implement Frontend Artist Profile Management and Image Upload Dashboard\",\n836\t      \"description\": \"Build the artist profile editing dashboard UI allowing creators to update stage name, bio, social links, and upload avatar/header banner images. Features drag-and-drop file uploaders with image preview cropped ratios, real-time character counters, and inline validation error messages.\",\n837\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n838\t        \"Provides form controls for editing stageName, bio (with 500-char counter), and up to 5 social links with platform selectors.\",\n839\t        \"Includes file input uploaders for avatar (1:1 crop preview) and header banner (16:9 crop preview) with 5MB file size validation.\",\n840\t        \"Submits image uploads to /api/v1/artist-profile/avatar and /header and metadata changes to PATCH /api/v1/artist-profile.\",\n841\t        \"Displays toast notifications on successful save or inline error alerts on 422 response validation failures.\",\n842\t        \"Unit tests in src/components/ArtistProfileEditor.test.tsx test preview generation, char counter math, and form submission.\",\n843\t        \"Playwright spec in e2e/tests/artist-profile-edit.spec.ts covers modifying bio text, selecting avatar image, and saving profile changes.\"\n844\t      ],\n845\t      \"priority\": 39,\n846\t      \"passes\": false,\n847\t      \"dependsOn\": [\n848\t        \"STORY-profile-002\",\n849\t        \"STORY-profile-003\",\n850\t        \"STORY-setup-003\"\n851\t      ],\n852\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n853\t      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n854\t      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n855\t    },\n856\t    {\n857\t      \"id\": \"STORY-profile-008\",\n858\t      \"title\": \"Implement Frontend Public Listener Profile Page\",\n859\t      \"description\": \"Construct the public listener profile page (/users/[userId]) displaying user avatar, registration year, public playlists grid, and followed artists carousel. Renders public playlist cards showing cover mosaics and track counts, alongside a horizontal slider of followed artists.\",\n860\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n861\t        \"Renders header section with user avatar, username, and registration year.\",\n862\t        \"Displays Public Playlists Grid showing cards for playlists where isPublic is true, featuring cover art mosaic, title, and track count.\",\n863\t        \"Renders Followed Artists Carousel allowing horizontal scroll through followed creator cards.\",\n864\t        \"Complies with WCAG 2.1 AA keyboard accessibility and responsive layout guidelines down to 375px viewports per constraint [5].\",\n865\t        \"Unit tests in src/pages/ListenerProfileView.test.tsx verify playlist grid rendering and followed artists carousel structure.\",\n866\t        \"Playwright spec in e2e/tests/listener-profile.spec.ts tests loading a listener profile page and clicking a public playlist card.\"\n867\t      ],\n868\t      \"priority\": 40,\n869\t      \"passes\": false,\n870\t      \"dependsOn\": [\n871\t        \"STORY-profile-004\",\n872\t        \"STORY-setup-003\"\n873\t      ],\n874\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n875\t      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n876\t      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n877\t    },\n878\t    {\n879\t      \"id\": \"STORY-track-001\",\n880\t      \"title\": \"Implement Track Upload Intent API Endpoint with Presigned URL Generation\",\n881\t      \"description\": \"Develop the POST /api/v1/tracks/upload-intent endpoint validating media file parameters and issuing direct-to-storage presigned PUT URLs per DEC-008. Validates audio size (max 50MB per constraint [1]), audio MIME type (audio/mpeg, audio/wav), cover size (max 5MB), and returns short-lived S3/R2 presigned upload tokens.\",\n882\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n883\t        \"POST /api/v1/tracks/upload-intent checks requireVerifiedEmail gating rule and ARTIST role context.\",\n884\t        \"Enforces max 50MB (52,428,800 bytes) audio file limit and audio/mpeg or audio/wav MIME types per constraint [1].\",\n885\t        \"Enforces max 5MB cover image limit and image/jpeg, image/png, or image/webp MIME types.\",\n886\t        \"Returns HTTP 200 OK with audioUploadUrl (15-min presigned PUT URL), audioStorageKey, optional coverImageUploadUrl/Key, and UTC ISO-8601 expiresAt timestamp.\",\n887\t        \"Unit tests in src/services/uploadIntent.test.ts verify MIME type validation, file size checks, and presigned URL parameters.\",\n888\t        \"Integration test calls POST /api/v1/tracks/upload-intent with valid payload and asserts response key formats and 200 status.\"\n889\t      ],\n890\t      \"priority\": 41,\n891\t      \"passes\": false,\n892\t      \"dependsOn\": [\n893\t        \"STORY-role-004\",\n894\t        \"STORY-storage-002\"\n895\t      ],\n896\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n897\t      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n898\t      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n899\t    },\n900\t    {\n901\t      \"id\": \"STORY-track-002\",\n902\t      \"title\": \"Implement Server-Side Audio Metadata Extraction and Binary Header Inspection Service\",\n903\t      \"description\": \"Build an out-of-band audio processing service that inspects uploaded binary audio streams in storage to extract metadata. Reads headers to verify codec integrity, channel count, sample rate, bitrate, and precise duration in float seconds, detecting corrupted or spoofed audio files.\",\n904\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n905\t        \"Service connects via StorageProvider interface to read initial audio binary header bytes from storage.\",\n906\t        \"Extracts precise track duration in float seconds (e.g. 218.42), bitrate, sample rate, and channel topology.\",\n907\t        \"Verifies container format matches declared MIME type (MP3 or WAV per constraint [1]).\",\n908\t        \"Throws a typed CorruptedAudioError if the file header is unparseable, incomplete, or corrupted.\",\n909\t        \"Unit tests in src/services/audioMetadata.test.ts cover valid MP3/WAV header parsing and corrupted file detection.\",\n910\t        \"Integration test executes metadata extraction against sample audio files in local test storage.\"\n911\t      ],\n912\t      \"priority\": 42,\n913\t      \"passes\": false,\n914\t      \"dependsOn\": [\n915\t        \"STORY-storage-001\"\n916\t      ],\n917\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n918\t      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n919\t      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n920\t    },\n921\t    {\n922\t      \"id\": \"STORY-track-003\",\n923\t      \"title\": \"Implement Track Registration API Endpoint with Auto-Live Status and Cover Image Linking\",\n924\t      \"description\": \"Create the POST /api/v1/tracks registration endpoint to finalize track publishing. Invokes the audio metadata extraction service, sets status to LIVE per auto-live decision DEC-001, assigns cover art (or fallback genre default), persists the Track document in MongoDB via Prisma, and returns the track payload.\",\n925\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n926\t        \"POST /api/v1/tracks validates title (1-100 chars), genre (normalized taxonomy), and audioStorageKey presence.\",\n927\t        \"Triggers out-of-band audio duration extraction and stores floating-point seconds on Track.duration.\",\n928\t        \"Sets Track.status to 'LIVE' automatically per DEC-001 without requiring pre-upload admin approval.\",\n929\t        \"Links provided coverImageStorageKey or assigns default genre cover URL /static/covers/defaults/{genre}.png if omitted.\",\n930\t        \"Returns HTTP 201 Created with full Track object containing UTC ISO-8601 timestamps per constraint [0].\",\n931\t        \"Unit tests in src/services/trackRegistration.test.ts verify auto-live assignment, default cover art fallback, and metadata persistence.\",\n932\t        \"Integration test calls POST /api/v1/tracks with valid keys and asserts 201 status and DB Track record.\"\n933\t      ],\n934\t      \"priority\": 43,\n935\t      \"passes\": false,\n936\t      \"dependsOn\": [\n937\t        \"STORY-track-001\",\n938\t        \"STORY-track-002\"\n939\t      ],\n940\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n941\t      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n942\t      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n943\t    },\n944\t    {\n945\t      \"id\": \"STORY-track-004\",\n946\t      \"title\": \"Implement Genre Tagging Validation and Search Indexing Trigger Service\",\n947\t      \"description\": \"Implement genre validation against the normalized platform taxonomy (INDIE_ROCK, BEDROOM_POP, ELECTRONIC, HIP_HOP, LO_FI, AMBIENT, R_AND_B, FOLK, OTHER) and event dispatching for search indexing. Triggers background search index updates and genre queue aggregation upon track creation.\",\n948\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n949\t        \"Validates genre field against platform taxonomy enum values, rejecting invalid genres with 422 INVALID_GENRE_TAG.\",\n950\t        \"Dispatches post-creation background event to index new track title, artist stageName, and genre in search layer.\",\n951\t        \"Appends new track ID to the rule-based genre recommendation queue upon database insertion.\",\n952\t        \"Unit tests in src/services/genreIndexing.test.ts cover taxonomy validation and indexing event payload creation.\",\n953\t        \"Integration test verifies that creating a track fires the expected search indexing event trigger.\"\n954\t      ],\n955\t      \"priority\": 44,\n956\t      \"passes\": false,\n957\t      \"dependsOn\": [\n958\t        \"STORY-track-003\"\n959\t      ],\n960\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n961\t      \"effort\": \"small\",\n962\t      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n963\t    },\n964\t    {\n965\t      \"id\": \"STORY-track-005\",\n966\t      \"title\": \"Implement Storage Cleanup and Error Recovery Handlers for Upload Failures\",\n967\t      \"description\": \"Develop error recovery workflows for corrupt audio files or failed registration payloads. If audio header parsing fails or validation errors occur during track registration, executes automatic StorageProvider.deleteObject calls for orphan storage keys and returns HTTP 422 CORRUPTED_AUDIO_FILE.\",\n968\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n969\t        \"If audio metadata extraction fails or header is corrupted, invokes StorageProvider.deleteObject on audioStorageKey and coverImageStorageKey.\",\n970\t        \"Returns HTTP 422 Unprocessable Entity with error code CORRUPTED_AUDIO_FILE.\",\n971\t        \"Handles missing storage key errors during registration by returning HTTP 404 STORAGE_KEY_NOT_FOUND.\",\n972\t        \"Logs failure events with sanitized PII metadata for monitoring per cross-cutting guidelines sec-025.\",\n973\t        \"Unit tests in src/services/uploadErrorRecovery.test.ts verify storage deletion invocation and error envelope generation.\",\n974\t        \"Integration test simulates corrupted file header and verifies storage cleanup execution and 422 response.\"\n975\t      ],\n976\t      \"priority\": 45,\n977\t      \"passes\": false,\n978\t      \"dependsOn\": [\n979\t        \"STORY-track-003\",\n980\t        \"STORY-storage-001\"\n981\t      ],\n982\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n983\t      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n984\t      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n985\t    },\n986\t    {\n987\t      \"id\": \"STORY-track-006\",\n988\t      \"title\": \"Implement Frontend Track Upload Page and Interactive Multi-Step Upload Form\",\n989\t      \"description\": \"Construct the frontend creator track upload page (/dashboard/upload) featuring file drag-and-drop pickers, direct presigned S3/R2 upload execution with real-time percentage progress bar, metadata entry form (title, genre, description, cover image), and auto-live success redirect.\",\n990\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n991\t        \"Renders drag-and-drop file upload zone enforcing client-side max 50MB size and MP3/WAV format checks per constraint [1].\",\n992\t        \"Executes two-step upload flow: calls /upload-intent API, issues direct PUT request to presigned URL with visual progress bar, then submits metadata to /api/v1/tracks.\",\n993\t        \"Provides form inputs for track title (1-100 chars), genre dropdown (platform taxonomy), description (max 500 chars), and cover art image picker.\",\n994\t        \"Complies with WCAG 2.1 AA accessibility guidelines with aria-valuenow on progress bars and screen reader status updates per constraint [5].\",\n995\t        \"Displays clear error banner and retry action if upload or metadata processing fails.\",\n996\t        \"Unit tests in src/components/TrackUploadWizard.test.tsx test file drag-and-drop validation, upload progress calculation, and form submission.\",\n997\t        \"Playwright spec in e2e/tests/track-upload.spec.ts tests picking an MP3 file, filling metadata, uploading, and verifying redirect to published track view.\"\n998\t      ],\n999\t      \"priority\": 46,\n1000\t      \"passes\": false,\n1001\t      \"dependsOn\": [\n1002\t        \"STORY-track-001\",\n1003\t        \"STORY-track-003\",\n1004\t        \"STORY-storage-004\",\n1005\t        \"STORY-setup-003\"\n1006\t      ],\n1007\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n1008\t      \"effort\": \"high\",\n1009\t      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n1010\t    },\n1011\t    {\n1012\t      \"id\": \"STORY-track-007\",\n1013\t      \"title\": \"Implement Track Metadata Update API Endpoint and Payload Validation\",\n1014\t      \"description\": \"Create the REST API endpoint PATCH /api/v1/tracks/[id] allowing Artists and Admins to modify track title, coverImageUrl, and genre tag. Enforce server-side identity and ownership verification, validate payload fields, reject immutable field edit attempts with HTTP 422 IMMUTABLE_FIELD_REJECTED, and trigger tag-based cache revalidation.\",\n1015\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n1016\t        \"PATCH /api/v1/tracks/[id] requires authentication and Artist or Admin role, returning 403 ARTIST_PROFILE_REQUIRED if requesting user has no associated ArtistProfile.\",\n1017\t        \"Server compares Track.artistProfileId against user's ArtistProfile.id, returning HTTP 403 Forbidden with code FORBIDDEN_OWNERSHIP_MISMATCH if mismatched and user is not Admin.\",\n1018\t        \"Payload validation accepts optional title (1-100 characters, trimmed), coverImageUrl (valid HTTP/S URL under 5MB), and genre (matching allowed system genre taxonomy).\",\n1019\t        \"Including any immutable field (audioUrl, duration, playCount, likeCount, artistProfileId) in the request body triggers HTTP 422 Unprocessable Entity with code IMMUTABLE_FIELD_REJECTED.\",\n1020\t        \"Successful metadata updates mutate database record, set updatedAt in UTC ISO-8601 format, revalidate cache tags (track-[id], artist-catalog-[artistProfileId], genre-feed-[genre]), and return 200 OK with updated metadata.\",\n1021\t        \"Admin-initiated metadata edits emit an immutable entry to AuditLog capturing admin user ID, track ID, and modified fields.\",\n1022\t        \"Integration tests in tests/api/track-update.test.ts call PATCH /api/v1/tracks/[id] with valid owner payload (asserts 200), immutable payload (asserts 422), unauthorized user (asserts 403), and non-existent track (asserts 404).\"\n1023\t      ],\n1024\t      \"priority\": 47,\n1025\t      \"passes\": false,\n1026\t      \"dependsOn\": [\n1027\t        \"STORY-setup-006\",\n1028\t        \"STORY-track-003\",\n1029\t        \"STORY-security-005\"\n1030\t      ],\n1031\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n1032\t      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n1033\t      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n1034\t    },\n1035\t    {\n1036\t      \"id\": \"STORY-track-008\",\n1037\t      \"title\": \"Implement Asynchronous Storage Cleanup for Replaced Track Cover Art\",\n1038\t      \"description\": \"Create an asynchronous storage cleanup background job triggered when a track's coverImageUrl is updated via PATCH /api/v1/tracks/[id]. Extract the previous cover image key and execute StorageProvider.deleteFile() out-of-band to prevent storage waste.\",\n1039\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n1040\t        \"When PATCH /api/v1/tracks/[id] updates coverImageUrl to a new URL, the handler enqueues a background task with the previous cover art storage key.\",\n1041\t        \"Asynchronous job invokes StorageProvider.deleteFile(key) to permanently delete the orphaned cover image asset from object storage (S3/R2).\",\n1042\t        \"If coverImageUrl is omitted or unchanged in the update payload, no storage deletion job is enqueued.\",\n1043\t        \"Storage provider deletion failures are logged as structured errors and retried without blocking or failing the HTTP PATCH response.\",\n1044\t        \"Unit tests in tests/unit/cover-art-cleanup.test.ts verify that StorageProvider.deleteFile() is called with the exact previous key when coverImageUrl changes.\"\n1045\t      ],\n1046\t      \"priority\": 48,\n1047\t      \"passes\": false,\n1048\t      \"dependsOn\": [\n1049\t        \"STORY-track-007\",\n1050\t        \"STORY-storage-001\"\n1051\t      ],\n1052\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n1053\t      \"effort\": \"small\",\n1054\t      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n1055\t    },\n1056\t    {\n1057\t      \"id\": \"STORY-track-009\",\n1058\t      \"title\": \"Implement Track Soft Archival Deletion Endpoint and Stream Interceptor\",\n1059\t      \"description\": \"Create the DELETE /api/v1/tracks/[id] endpoint to soft-delete tracks by setting deletedAt to the current UTC ISO-8601 timestamp and status to archived. Update streaming route handlers to intercept requests for soft-deleted tracks and return HTTP 404 TRACK_ARCHIVED.\",\n1060\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n1061\t        \"DELETE /api/v1/tracks/[id] requires authentication and ownership verification (or Admin role), returning 403 FORBIDDEN_OWNERSHIP_MISMATCH on mismatch.\",\n1062\t        \"Successful deletion updates Track.deletedAt to current UTC ISO-8601 timestamp and sets Track.status to archived.\",\n1063\t        \"Global data access queries enforce mandatory filter deletedAt: null, instantly hiding soft-deleted tracks from search, feeds, recommendations, artist profiles, and follower activity feeds.\",\n1064\t        \"GET /api/v1/tracks/[id]/stream checks deletedAt !== null or status === 'archived' and returns HTTP 404 with structured error body { \\\"error\\\": { \\\"code\\\": \\\"TRACK_ARCHIVED\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"This track is no longer available.\\\" } }.\",\n1065\t        \"Admin track soft-deletion emits an entry to AuditLog capturing admin ID, track ID, and timestamp.\",\n1066\t        \"Integration tests in tests/api/track-delete.test.ts verify soft-archival database state, 404 response on streaming archived track, and 403 on unauthorized deletion.\"\n1067\t      ],\n1068\t      \"priority\": 49,\n1069\t      \"passes\": false,\n1070\t      \"dependsOn\": [\n1071\t        \"STORY-setup-006\",\n1072\t        \"STORY-track-007\",\n1073\t        \"STORY-storage-003\"\n1074\t      ],\n1075\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n1076\t      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n1077\t      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n1078\t    },\n1079\t    {\n1080\t      \"id\": \"STORY-track-010\",\n1081\t      \"title\": \"Implement Synchronous Playlist Cascade Cleanup and Catalog Counter Sync\",\n1082\t      \"description\": \"Create a synchronous database cascade cleanup service executed during track soft-deletion. Purge all PlaylistTrack junction records referencing the track, re-index position ordering for remaining playlist items, decrement playlist track counts, and decrement artist total track count.\",\n1083\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n1084\t        \"Triggered synchronously within single database transaction during DELETE /api/v1/tracks/[id] processing.\",\n1085\t        \"Executes batch deletion of all PlaylistTrack junction records referencing the soft-deleted track ID.\",\n1086\t        \"Re-indexes remaining PlaylistTrack positions (position = position - 1 for position > deletedTrackPosition) per affected playlist.\",\n1087\t        \"Decrements trackCount metric on all affected Playlist records by 1.\",\n1088\t        \"Decrements trackCount metric on the track owner's ArtistProfile record by 1.\",\n1089\t        \"Invalidates cache tags for affected playlists and artist catalog listings.\",\n1090\t        \"Integration tests in tests/services/playlist-cascade.test.ts assert PlaylistTrack purge, position re-indexing without gaps, and accurate trackCount decrements on Playlist and ArtistProfile.\"\n1091\t      ],\n1092\t      \"priority\": 50,\n1093\t      \"passes\": false,\n1094\t      \"dependsOn\": [\n1095\t        \"STORY-track-009\"\n1096\t      ],\n1097\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n1098\t      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n1099\t      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n1100\t    },\n1101\t    {\n1102\t      \"id\": \"STORY-track-011\",\n1103\t      \"title\": \"Implement Asynchronous Storage Media Asset Purging Pipeline for Archived Tracks\",\n1104\t      \"description\": \"Implement the TrackMediaPurgeJob background task queue worker that permanently deletes physical audio (audioStorageKey) and cover image (coverStorageKey) files from object storage (S3/R2) following track soft-deletion.\",\n1105\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n1106\t        \"Triggered asynchronously via task queue event emitted after successful Track soft-deletion.\",\n1107\t        \"TrackMediaPurgeJob retrieves audioStorageKey and coverStorageKey for the archived track ID.\",\n1108\t        \"Invokes StorageProvider.deleteFile() for both the audio binary asset and cover image asset.\",\n1109\t        \"Handles missing keys or storage API failures with exponential backoff retries and structured error logging.\",\n1110\t        \"Preserves database record in archived state for analytical history while confirming storage objects are purged.\",\n1111\t        \"Unit and integration tests in tests/jobs/track-media-purge.test.ts verify worker invocation, target storage key deletion calls, and error retry handling.\"\n1112\t      ],\n1113\t      \"priority\": 51,\n1114\t      \"passes\": false,\n1115\t      \"dependsOn\": [\n1116\t        \"STORY-track-009\",\n1117\t        \"STORY-storage-001\"\n1118\t      ],\n1119\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n1120\t      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n1121\t      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n1122\t    },\n1123\t    {\n1124\t      \"id\": \"STORY-track-012\",\n1125\t      \"title\": \"Implement Frontend Artist Catalog Management Page and Track Edit Form\",\n1126\t      \"description\": \"Build the artist catalog management interface and interactive track metadata edit modal using Next.js, React Hook Form, and shadcn/ui. Enable artists to view uploaded tracks and edit title, cover artwork URL/file, and genre tag with real-time feedback.\",\n1127\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n1128\t        \"Renders artist catalog list displaying track artwork, title, genre badge, upload timestamp, play count, and Edit/Delete action controls.\",\n1129\t        \"Clicking Edit opens a modal dialog pre-populated with current title, cover image, and genre dropdown matching system taxonomy.\",\n1130\t        \"Validates form inputs displaying inline errors for title (1-100 characters) and invalid cover image URLs or files over 5MB.\",\n1131\t        \"Submitting form calls PATCH /api/v1/tracks/[id] and updates catalog list UI state and Next.js revalidated data upon 200 OK success response.\",\n1132\t        \"Modal and form elements satisfy WCAG 2.1 AA accessibility guidelines (keyboard focus trapping, ARIA dialog labels, visible focus rings).\",\n1133\t        \"Playwright spec in e2e/tests/artist-catalog-edit.spec.ts verifies opening edit modal, modifying title and genre, submitting valid form, and asserting updated UI listing.\"\n1134\t      ],\n1135\t      \"priority\": 52,\n1136\t      \"passes\": false,\n1137\t      \"dependsOn\": [\n1138\t        \"STORY-track-007\",\n1139\t        \"STORY-profile-007\"\n1140\t      ],\n1141\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n1142\t      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n1143\t      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n1144\t    },\n1145\t    {\n1146\t      \"id\": \"STORY-track-013\",\n1147\t      \"title\": \"Implement Frontend Track Deletion Dialog and Active Player Queue Synchronization\",\n1148\t      \"description\": \"Build the track deletion confirmation dialog in the artist catalog dashboard and implement real-time player bar and queue state synchronization when an actively playing or queued track is edited or soft-deleted.\",\n1149\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n1150\t        \"Clicking Delete in artist catalog opens a confirmation dialog warning that soft-archiving removes the track from user playlists.\",\n1151\t        \"Confirming deletion calls DELETE /api/v1/tracks/[id] and removes track row from artist catalog UI upon 200 OK.\",\n1152\t        \"If active playing track metadata is modified by the artist, persistent player bar updates title and artwork seamlessly without interrupting playback.\",\n1153\t        \"If actively playing/queued track is deleted, browser audio buffer plays to completion, player marks queue item unavailable, displays toast notification ('Track removed by artist'), and advances to next valid queue item.\",\n1154\t        \"Confirmation dialog and player alerts comply with WCAG 2.1 AA keyboard accessibility and screen reader announcement standards (aria-live).\",\n1155\t        \"Playwright spec in e2e/tests/artist-catalog-delete.spec.ts covers deletion dialog confirmation, catalog item removal, and player toast notification trigger on active track deletion.\"\n1156\t      ],\n1157\t      \"priority\": 53,\n1158\t      \"passes\": false,\n1159\t      \"dependsOn\": [\n1160\t        \"STORY-track-009\",\n1161\t        \"STORY-track-012\"\n1162\t      ],\n1163\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n1164\t      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n1165\t      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n1166\t    },\n1167\t    {\n1168\t      \"id\": \"STORY-player-001\",\n1169\t      \"title\": \"Implement Audio Player React Context and Session Persistence Provider\",\n1170\t      \"description\": \"Create the AudioPlayerProvider React context wrapper in app/layout.tsx above child page routes. The provider maintains global player state, encapsulates a hidden HTML5 audio element, exposes useAudioPlayer(), and persists session metadata to browser sessionStorage under indie_player_session for seamless state restoration on tab reloads.\",\n1171\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n1172\t        \"AudioPlayerProvider is mounted in app/layout.tsx root layout and exposes useAudioPlayer() context hook to all child page routes.\",\n1173\t        \"Player state encapsulates PlaybackStatus ('IDLE', 'LOADING', 'BUFFERING', 'PLAYING', 'PAUSED', 'ERROR'), currentTrack metadata, currentTime, duration, volume, isMuted, repeatMode ('OFF', 'ALL', 'ONE'), and isShuffleActive.\",\n1174\t        \"A hidden HTML5 <audio> element is mounted inside AudioPlayerProvider and abstracts native events (timeupdate, ended, waiting, playing, error, stalled) into application state updates.\",\n1175\t        \"Active track and queue state are automatically mirrored to sessionStorage under key indie_player_session upon state changes.\",\n1176\t        \"On tab reload, the provider restores track metadata and seek timestamp from indie_player_session in a PAUSED state without triggering immediate auto-play.\",\n1177\t        \"Unit tests in context/AudioPlayerContext.test.tsx verify state transitions, event subscriptions, and sessionStorage serialization.\",\n1178\t        \"Playwright spec in e2e/tests/player-persistence.spec.ts verifies player state remains active across client-side page route navigation.\"\n1179\t      ],\n1180\t      \"priority\": 54,\n1181\t      \"passes\": false,\n1182\t      \"dependsOn\": [\n1183\t        \"STORY-setup-002\",\n1184\t        \"STORY-setup-003\"\n1185\t      ],\n1186\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n1187\t      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n1188\t      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n1189\t    },\n1190\t    {\n1191\t      \"id\": \"STORY-player-002\",\n1192\t      \"title\": \"Implement Audio Player Queue State Engine and Shuffling Actions\",\n1193\t      \"description\": \"Implement in-memory queue management logic inside AudioPlayerProvider with a hard cap of 500 items. Provides queue manipulation actions including immediate track play with context queue, insertion next, appending to queue end, drag-and-drop reordering, Fisher-Yates shuffle toggle preserving original queue order, and repeat mode management.\",\n1194\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n1195\t        \"Queue state maintains originalQueue, activeQueue, historyStack, and currentIndex with an enforced maximum limit of 500 items.\",\n1196\t        \"playTrackImmediately(track, contextQueue) loads target track, updates activeQueue with context queue if supplied, and sets currentIndex.\",\n1197\t        \"insertQueueNext(tracks) appends target tracks directly after currentIndex, while addToQueueEnd(tracks) appends items to the end of activeQueue.\",\n1198\t        \"playNextTrack() and playPreviousTrack() correctly navigate activeQueue, handling historyStack pops and repeatMode ('OFF', 'ALL', 'ONE') boundaries.\",\n1199\t        \"toggleShuffle() creates a randomized permutation of activeQueue items following currentIndex using the Fisher-Yates algorithm while preserving originalQueue.\",\n1200\t        \"Disabling shuffle restores activeQueue to originalQueue while matching currentIndex to the currently active track.\",\n1201\t        \"Unit tests in utils/queueEngine.test.ts cover queue insertion, reordering, Fisher-Yates shuffle integrity, and repeat mode boundary conditions.\"\n1202\t      ],\n1203\t      \"priority\": 55,\n1204\t      \"passes\": false,\n1205\t      \"dependsOn\": [\n1206\t        \"STORY-player-001\"\n1207\t      ],\n1208\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n1209\t      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n1210\t      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n1211\t    },\n1212\t    {\n1213\t      \"id\": \"STORY-player-003\",\n1214\t      \"title\": \"Implement Persistent Bottom Audio Player Bar UI Component\",\n1215\t      \"description\": \"Build the persistent AudioPlayerBar component fixed to the bottom of the viewport in root layout. Features track cover art and title display, play/pause controls, seek progress slider with visual drag jitter protection, volume slider with logarithmic scaling, mute toggle, and retry handling for stream buffering and network errors.\",\n1216\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n1217\t        \"AudioPlayerBar component is rendered in app/layout.tsx and styled with fixed bottom positioning using dark-mode design system tokens.\",\n1218\t        \"Displays current track cover art, track title, artist name, current seek position, and total duration formatted as MM:SS.\",\n1219\t        \"Seek slider supports click-jump and drag scrubbing, pausing timeupdate event updates during drag to eliminate thumb jitter.\",\n1220\t        \"Volume slider maps normalized float (0.0-1.0) to audio element volume using logarithmic formula V_effective = V^2.5 and persists setting under localStorage key indie_player_volume.\",\n1221\t        \"Toggling mute silences output while preserving previous volume level for restoration upon unmute.\",\n1222\t        \"Stream errors trigger up to 3 retry attempts with exponential backoff (1s, 2s, 4s) before showing a non-blocking toast error in player UI.\",\n1223\t        \"Component unit tests in components/player/AudioPlayerBar.test.tsx verify play/pause toggles, volume scaling, seek events, and error UI states.\",\n1224\t        \"Playwright spec in e2e/tests/player-bar.spec.ts verifies audio playback controls and volume persistence.\"\n1225\t      ],\n1226\t      \"priority\": 56,\n1227\t      \"passes\": false,\n1228\t      \"dependsOn\": [\n1229\t        \"STORY-player-001\"\n1230\t      ],\n1231\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n1232\t      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n1233\t      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n1234\t    },\n1235\t    {\n1236\t      \"id\": \"STORY-player-004\",\n1237\t      \"title\": \"Implement Slide-Out Queue Drawer Overlay Component\",\n1238\t      \"description\": \"Build the slide-out queue overlay panel component toggled from the player bar. Displays the current track, upcoming queued tracks, track durations, drag-and-drop item reordering controls, track removal buttons, and a clear queue action.\",\n1239\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n1240\t        \"Slide-out queue panel opens via a queue toggle button on AudioPlayerBar with accessible overlay backdrop.\",\n1241\t        \"Renders currently playing track highlight alongside the scrollable list of activeQueue items.\",\n1242\t        \"Supports drag-and-drop repositioning of queued tracks, calling reorderQueue(startIndex, endIndex) without interrupting active playback.\",\n1243\t        \"Individual tracks can be removed via a delete button, triggering removeFromQueue(index).\",\n1244\t        \"Clear queue button empties activeQueue up to the current playing track and updates queue drawer state.\",\n1245\t        \"Component unit tests in components/player/QueueDrawer.test.tsx verify render list, drag reordering triggers, and clear queue button actions.\",\n1246\t        \"Playwright spec in e2e/tests/queue-drawer.spec.ts verifies opening the drawer, reordering items, and removing tracks.\"\n1247\t      ],\n1248\t      \"priority\": 57,\n1249\t      \"passes\": false,\n1250\t      \"dependsOn\": [\n1251\t        \"STORY-player-002\",\n1252\t        \"STORY-player-003\"\n1253\t      ],\n1254\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n1255\t      \"effort\": \"small\",\n1256\t      \"model\": \"haiku\"\n1257\t    },\n1258\t    {\n1259\t      \"id\": \"STORY-player-005\",\n1260\t      \"title\": \"Implement MediaSession API Integration and Platform Keyboard Shortcuts\",\n1261\t      \"description\": \"Integrate the browser navigator.MediaSession API to sync playback state and metadata with OS hardware media controls. Implement platform-wide keyboard hotkeys for play/pause, seek, volume, and track skip, along with WCAG 2.1 AA ARIA attributes and screen reader announcements.\",\n1262\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n1263\t        \"navigator.mediaSession.metadata is updated on track load with title, artist, album name, and cover artwork variants (96x96, 256x256, 512x512).\",\n1264\t        \"Binds MediaSession action handlers for play, pause, previoustrack, nexttrack, seekto, and stop.\",\n1265\t        \"Global keyboard hotkeys are active platform-wide: Space/K (Play/Pause), M (Mute), Left/Right Arrows (5s seek), J/L (10s seek), Shift+N/P (Next/Prev track).\",\n1266\t        \"Keyboard shortcuts are automatically suppressed when user focus resides inside input fields, textareas, or select dropdowns.\",\n1267\t        \"Seek and volume sliders include role='slider', aria-valuenow, aria-valuemin, aria-valuemax, aria-valuetext, and 2px high-contrast focus rings.\",\n1268\t        \"An aria-live='polite' screen reader region announces track changes ('Now playing: Track Title by Artist Name').\",\n1269\t        \"Unit tests in hooks/useMediaSession.test.tsx and hooks/usePlayerHotkeys.test.tsx cover event binding and input suppression logic.\",\n1270\t        \"Playwright spec in e2e/tests/player-accessibility.spec.ts verifies hotkey execution and ARIA slider attributes.\"\n1271\t      ],\n1272\t      \"priority\": 58,\n1273\t      \"passes\": false,\n1274\t      \"dependsOn\": [\n1275\t        \"STORY-player-001\",\n1276\t        \"STORY-player-003\"\n1277\t      ],\n1278\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n1279\t      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n1280\t      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n1281\t    },\n1282\t    {\n1283\t      \"id\": \"STORY-player-006\",\n1284\t      \"title\": \"Implement Unauthenticated Guest Playback and Auth Prompt Interceptor\",\n1285\t      \"description\": \"Ensure unauthenticated guest users can stream public tracks and public playlists without login tokens. Add an authentication modal trigger interceptor when guest users click interactive social buttons (Like, Follow, Save) on the persistent player bar UI without halting active playback.\",\n1286\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n1287\t        \"Guest users can stream public tracks using signed GET media delivery URLs without requiring auth tokens.\",\n1288\t        \"Guest player bar maintains session queue and volume preferences in sessionStorage and localStorage.\",\n1289\t        \"Clicking 'Like Track', 'Follow Artist', or 'Save to Playlist' from the player bar while unauthenticated triggers the auth prompt modal.\",\n1290\t        \"Audio playback continues uninterrupted in background while the auth prompt modal is visible.\",\n1291\t        \"Unit tests in components/player/GuestAuthInterceptor.test.tsx verify social action interception for guests.\",\n1292\t        \"Playwright spec in e2e/tests/guest-playback.spec.ts verifies unauthenticated track playback and auth modal trigger.\"\n1293\t      ],\n1294\t      \"priority\": 59,\n1295\t      \"passes\": false,\n1296\t      \"dependsOn\": [\n1297\t        \"STORY-player-001\",\n1298\t        \"STORY-player-003\"\n1299\t      ],\n1300\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n1301\t      \"effort\": \"small\",\n1302\t      \"model\": \"haiku\"\n1303\t    },\n1304\t    {\n1305\t      \"id\": \"STORY-listen-001\",\n1306\t      \"title\": \"Implement Play Session Initialization API Endpoint\",\n1307\t      \"description\": \"Create the POST /api/v1/tracks/:id/play-session API endpoint that issues a time-bound HMAC-SHA256 signed playbackToken containing trackId, sessionId, issuedAt, and requiredThresholdSeconds calculated as min(30s, 0.5 * duration).\",\n1308\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n1309\t        \"Endpoint POST /api/v1/tracks/:id/play-session accepts trackId parameter and returns 200 OK with PlaySessionResponse.\",\n1310\t        \"Calculates requiredThresholdSeconds as min(30, 0.5 * Track.duration) based on database Track record.\","}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c7cf17ba-850b-408f-b83c-04ea23e5a468","uuid":"e48bb65f-240c-4df5-88cf-5fa1304aec8e","timestamp":"2026-08-03T14:18:57.811Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/surindersingh/ralph-workspaces/c9072b42-b87d-41f9-9f84-52cd1a37673c/dc5ea6e0-6839-4a4b-bc1c-d7416cac73af/prd.json","content":"{\n  \"branchName\": \"iotahub/phase-1\",\n  \"userStories\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"STORY-setup-001\",\n      \"title\": \"Initialize repository workspace git config and project root files\",\n      \"description\": \"Create the root repository workspace structure including git initialization, comprehensive .gitignore for Node and Next.js, README.md, .editorconfig, and root package.json. Defines the foundational workspace environment for subsequent scaffolding stories.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"Repository root contains initialized `.git` directory and clean working tree.\",\n        \"`.gitignore` exists covering `node_modules`, `.next`, `.env`, and build artifacts.\",\n        \"`.editorconfig` specifies 2-space indentation, UTF-8 encoding, and LF line endings.\",\n        \"`README.md` documents repository layout, setup prerequisites, and development scripts.\",\n        \"Root `package.json` initializes project name as `spotify` with private package status.\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 0,\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"dependsOn\": [],\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"effort\": \"small\",\n      \"model\": \"haiku\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"STORY-setup-002\",\n      \"title\": \"Scaffold Next.js 14 fullstack monolith project baseline\",\n      \"description\": \"Scaffold a Next.js 14 App Router project with TypeScript 5.x support in the root directory. Configures strict TypeScript compiler options, App Router directory layout (`/app`), and basic page/layout entrypoints.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"Next.js 14 App Router project initialized with TypeScript 5.x configuration in root directory.\",\n        \"`tsconfig.json` enforces `strict: true`, `target: ES2022`, and path aliases `@/*` pointing to `./src/*`.\",\n        \"`app/layout.tsx` and `app/page.tsx` exist as minimal functional React Server Components.\",\n        \"Running `npm run build` completes with exit code 0 and produces optimized standalone build output.\",\n        \"Running `npm run dev` boots Next.js development server on `http://localhost:3000` without runtime errors.\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 1,\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"STORY-setup-001\"\n      ],\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"effort\": \"small\",\n      \"model\": \"haiku\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"STORY-setup-003\",\n      \"title\": \"Install core dependencies and configure Tailwind CSS with shadcn UI\",\n      \"description\": \"Install Tailwind CSS 3.4+, Radix UI primitives, shadcn/ui integration, lucide-react icons, and music-metadata. Sets up dark-mode first HSL design tokens, responsive grid defaults down to 375px viewports, and utility styling classes.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"Dependencies `@radix-ui/react-slot`, `clsx`, `tailwind-merge`, `lucide-react`, `music-metadata` installed in `package.json`.\",\n        \"`tailwind.config.js` configures dark mode, HSL color tokens, typography scales, and content paths for `/src`.\",\n        \"`src/app/globals.css` defines CSS custom properties for dark-first HSL palette and WCAG AA contrast levels.\",\n        \"`components.json` configured for shadcn/ui primitive component auto-generation.\",\n        \"Unit test verifies helper utility `cn()` correctly merges Tailwind CSS classes.\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 2,\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"STORY-setup-002\"\n      ],\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"effort\": \"small\",\n      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"STORY-setup-004\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement MongoDB database schema and Prisma ORM models\",\n      \"description\": \"Configure Prisma ORM v5.x with MongoDB provider. Implement all 8 core canonical models (User, ArtistProfile, Track, Playlist, PlaylistTrack, Like, Follow, Report, AuditLog) and required enums, compound unique indexes, and relational attributes.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"`prisma/schema.prisma` created with MongoDB provider and 8 canonical models matching exact field specifications.\",\n        \"Enums `UserRole`, `AccountStatus`, `TrackStatus`, `Genre`, `ReportReason`, `ReportStatus`, and `AuditAction` defined.\",\n        \"Compound unique indexes `@unique([playlistId, position])`, `@unique([playlistId, trackId])`, `@unique([userId, trackId])`, `@unique([followerId, artistProfileId])` configured.\",\n        \"`npx prisma validate` succeeds and `npx prisma generate` outputs type-safe PrismaClient SDK.\",\n        \"Unit test instantiates PrismaClient and validates all model typings compile without TypeScript errors.\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 3,\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"STORY-setup-003\"\n      ],\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"STORY-setup-005\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement StorageService interface abstraction for S3 signed URLs\",\n      \"description\": \"Implement the vendor-agnostic `StorageService` interface wrapping `@aws-sdk/client-s3`. Provides methods for file upload, object deletion, and generating 60-minute presigned PUT upload URLs and 15-minute presigned GET stream delivery URLs.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"`StorageService` interface implemented in `src/lib/storage/storage.service.ts` with `uploadObject`, `deleteObject`, `generateSignedUrl`.\",\n        \"`S3StorageService` implementation handles AWS S3 / Cloudflare R2 compatible endpoint configurations.\",\n        \"`generateSignedUrl` enforces 3600-second TTL cap for `getObject` streaming requests.\",\n        \"Unit tests mock S3 client and verify correct presigned URL generation and parameter passing for `putObject` and `getObject`.\",\n        \"Integration test validates audio upload size constraint validation helper caps files at 50MB.\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 4,\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"STORY-setup-004\"\n      ],\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"STORY-setup-006\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement standardized REST API response wrappers and validation middleware\",\n      \"description\": \"Implement standard API JSON success and error outer envelopes, request ID tracing, UTC ISO-8601 timestamping, and a Zod schema validation middleware returning 422 Unprocessable Entity details arrays.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"Success helper `apiSuccessResponse(data, meta)` constructs payload with `success: true`, `data`, UTC timestamp, and `requestId`.\",\n        \"Error helper `apiErrorResponse(code, message, details)` constructs payload with `success: false`, `error` code, and optional `details` array.\",\n        \"Validation middleware `validateBody(schema)` validates Zod schema and returns HTTP 422 with `ValidationErrorDetail` format on failure.\",\n        \"Passwords and sensitive credentials are sanitized and excluded from error payload outputs and log traces.\",\n        \"Integration tests cover `apiSuccessResponse`, `apiErrorResponse`, and Zod validation failure scenarios for HTTP status codes 400, 422, and 500.\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 5,\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"STORY-setup-005\"\n      ],\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"STORY-setup-007\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement JWT authentication middleware and admin RBAC route guards\",\n      \"description\": \"Build server-side authentication middleware handling 7-day HTTP-only cookies containing JWT session tokens. Implement bcrypt cost-12 password hashing helpers and strict server-side RBAC middleware for `/api/v1/admin/*` and `/admin/*` routes.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"`hashPassword` and `comparePassword` utilities wrap `bcryptjs` using cost factor 12.\",\n        \"`generateToken` and `verifyToken` helpers handle 7-day JWT stateless session payloads.\",\n        \"Next.js `middleware.ts` intercepts `/admin/*` and `/api/v1/admin/*` routes, enforcing `ADMIN` user role server-side.\",\n        \"Unauthenticated requests to protected paths return HTTP 401 `UNAUTHENTICATED`, non-admin requests return HTTP 403 `FORBIDDEN_INSUFFICIENT_ROLE`.\",\n        \"Integration tests verify JWT session extraction from HTTP-only cookies and RBAC route protection for Listener vs Admin roles.\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 6,\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"STORY-setup-006\"\n      ],\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"STORY-setup-008\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement limit-offset pagination contracts and response helpers\",\n      \"description\": \"Create standard pagination parser and formatter utilities for REST collection endpoints. Enforces 1-indexed page numbers, default 20-item limits, 100-item maximum caps, and paginated API response JSON structures.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"`parsePaginationParams(url)` parses `page` (default 1) and `limit` (default 20, max 100).\",\n        \"`apiPaginatedResponse(data, total, page, limit)` returns JSON envelope containing `data[]`, `pagination` object (`total`, `page`, `limit`, `totalPages`, `hasNextPage`, `hasPreviousPage`), and `meta`.\",\n        \"`limit` values exceeding 100 are automatically clamped to 100.\",\n        \"Unit tests in `src/lib/api/pagination.test.ts` test default fallback, maximum clamping, and total page calculation math.\",\n        \"Integration test verifies query parameter parsing against a dummy collection route.\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 7,\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"STORY-setup-007\"\n      ],\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"effort\": \"small\",\n      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"STORY-setup-009\",\n      \"title\": \"Configure Vitest unit integration test runner and Playwright E2E setup\",\n      \"description\": \"Configure Vitest for server/service unit testing and Playwright for frontend E2E browser testing. Includes test scripts in `package.json`, environment setup, and baseline passing test suites.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"Vitest configured with `@testing-library/react` and Node.js environment in `vitest.config.ts`.\",\n        \"Playwright configured in `playwright.config.ts` targeting standard web viewports (desktop and 375px mobile).\",\n        \"`npm run test` executes Vitest unit/integration tests with exit code 0.\",\n        \"`npm run test:e2e` executes Playwright specs against running dev server with exit code 0.\",\n        \"Sample unit test `src/lib/sample.test.ts` and sample E2E spec `e2e/home.spec.ts` pass cleanly.\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 8,\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"STORY-setup-008\"\n      ],\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"STORY-setup-010\",\n      \"title\": \"Configure environment variable schema template and GitHub Actions CI workflow\",\n      \"description\": \"Create `.env.example` defining all required runtime secrets and setup a GitHub Actions CI pipeline running linting, TypeScript compilation, Prisma schema validation, Vitest unit tests, and Playwright E2E suites.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"`.env.example` created listing `DATABASE_URL`, `JWT_SECRET`, `AWS_REGION`, `AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID`, `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY`, `S3_BUCKET_NAME`, `S3_ENDPOINT`.\",\n        \"`src/lib/env.ts` implements Zod parsing for process.env at server startup.\",\n        \"`.github/workflows/ci.yml` created with steps: checkout, node setup, install dependencies, lint, typecheck, prisma validate, vitest run, playwright test.\",\n        \"Build fails in CI if TypeScript compilation contains errors or test coverage target is breached.\",\n        \"Manual execution of CI workflow steps locally succeeds cleanly.\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 9,\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"STORY-setup-009\"\n      ],\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"effort\": \"small\",\n      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"STORY-security-001\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement Bcrypt Password Hashing and Payload Sanitization Utility\",\n      \"description\": \"Create a backend security service using bcrypt with cost factor 12 and 16-byte random salt to hash user passwords prior to storage in MongoDB. Include automatic sanitization functions to strip passwordHash from Prisma database queries and API response payloads.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"Hashing passwords using bcrypt generates a valid salt and hash using cost factor 12.\",\n        \"Verifying a raw password against the stored hash returns true for correct input and false for invalid input.\",\n        \"Sanitization helper function strips passwordHash from User model objects before JSON serialization.\",\n        \"Prisma query select wrappers omit passwordHash from returned fields unless explicitly selected.\",\n        \"Password hashes are never written to standard log streams or error stack trace outputs per sec-024 sensitive data security rules.\",\n        \"Unit tests in tests/unit/security/password.test.ts verify hashing, cost factor 12 execution time (~250ms), verification logic, and payload sanitization.\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 10,\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"STORY-setup-004\"\n      ],\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"STORY-security-002\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement Session JWT Token Service and Secure Cookie Serialization\",\n      \"description\": \"Develop a stateless JWT session token management service that signs and verifies claims including userId, role, and optional artistProfileId using HMAC-SHA256. Configure HTTP-only, SameSite=Strict, Secure cookie serialization with a 7-day expiration under __Host-indie_session.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"JWT token generation includes userId, role ('LISTENER'|'ARTIST'|'ADMIN'), optional artistProfileId, iat, and exp claims signed with JWT_SECRET.\",\n        \"Session cookie serialization sets __Host-indie_session with HttpOnly: true, Secure: true, SameSite: Strict, Path: /, and Max-Age: 604800 (7 days).\",\n        \"Expired or tampered JWT signatures fail verification and throw a structured session invalidation error.\",\n        \"All timestamp claims (iat, exp) adhere to UTC ISO-8601 / Unix epoch standards in UTC per constraint 0.\",\n        \"Unit tests in tests/unit/security/session.test.ts cover token creation, claim validation, signature tampering, expiration checks, and cookie header formatting.\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 11,\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"STORY-setup-007\"\n      ],\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"STORY-security-003\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement Next.js Edge Middleware for Server-Side Route Guarding\",\n      \"description\": \"Build Next.js Edge Middleware in middleware.ts to intercept protected routes /admin/*, /api/v1/admin/*, /api/v1/artist/*, /api/v1/playlists/*, and /api/v1/reports/*. Verify session cookies, validate role hierarchy, and inject decoded identity claims into request headers.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"Unauthenticated requests targeting protected routes return HTTP status 401 Unauthorized.\",\n        \"Authenticated requests lacking required roles (e.g. Listener accessing /admin/*) return HTTP status 403 Forbidden per constraint 3.\",\n        \"Valid requests propagate decoded session claims in custom request headers x-user-id, x-user-role, and x-artist-profile-id to downstream handlers.\",\n        \"Public routes (such as guest search and track streaming) bypass middleware role checks per DEC-005.\",\n        \"Unit tests cover middleware claim parsing and route matcher logic.\",\n        \"Integration tests verify HTTP 401, 403, and header injection behavior for protected API routes.\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 12,\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"STORY-setup-007\",\n        \"STORY-security-002\"\n      ],\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"STORY-security-004\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement Resource Ownership Verification Helpers and IDOR Protection\",\n      \"description\": \"Implement reusable backend resource authorization functions to enforce Insecure Direct Object Reference (IDOR) protection in REST API route handlers. Ensure users can only modify or delete their own Track and Playlist records unless they hold the Admin role.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"Track ownership check confirms Track.artistProfileId equals caller's artistProfileId or caller holds ADMIN role.\",\n        \"Playlist ownership check confirms Playlist.userId equals caller's userId or caller holds ADMIN role.\",\n        \"Failed ownership checks abort execution and return HTTP 403 Forbidden with code ERR_RESOURCE_OWNERSHIP_DENIED and detailed resource info.\",\n        \"Admin role overrides ownership restrictions across all Track and Playlist update and delete handlers.\",\n        \"Integration tests assert HTTP 403 response structure when an unauthorized user attempts to edit another user's playlist or track.\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 13,\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"STORY-security-001\",\n        \"STORY-security-002\"\n      ],\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"STORY-security-005\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement Higher-Order withAuth and withRole API Handler Wrappers\",\n      \"description\": \"Create higher-order functions withAuth and withRole to wrap Next.js API handlers, extract session claims, build an immutable AuthContext, and handle authentication error responses uniformly.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"withAuth extracts claims from request headers injected by middleware or direct cookie verification and constructs immutable AuthContext.\",\n        \"withRole verifies that AuthContext.user.role matches one of the specified allowed roles for the route.\",\n        \"Token invalidation or expiry caught inside the wrapper returns HTTP 401 Unauthorized with standardized envelope error code ERR_UNAUTHORIZED.\",\n        \"Unit tests in tests/unit/security/wrappers.test.ts verify AuthContext injection and role boundary validation.\",\n        \"Integration tests confirm 401 error envelope format when calling wrapped endpoints without valid session headers.\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 14,\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"STORY-security-002\",\n        \"STORY-setup-006\"\n      ],\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"STORY-storage-001\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement Unified StorageProvider Interface for S3 and Cloudflare R2\",\n      \"description\": \"Build the StorageProvider abstraction layer utilizing AWS SDK v3 to support Amazon S3 and Cloudflare R2 object storage backends. Dynamically select provider implementation based on the STORAGE_PROVIDER environment variable.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"StorageProvider interface exposes generatePresignedUploadUrl, generatePresignedDownloadUrl, deleteObject, and getObjectMetadata.\",\n        \"System initializes AWS S3 or Cloudflare R2 client according to STORAGE_PROVIDER ('s3' or 'r2') environment configuration per DEC-008.\",\n        \"Presigned upload URLs generate valid S3/R2 PUT targets with specified TTL.\",\n        \"Presigned download URLs generate access-controlled GET targets with specified TTL.\",\n        \"Unit tests mock AWS SDK calls to test presigned URL creation, metadata reading, and object deletion.\",\n        \"Integration tests against mock S3 storage verify presigned upload token generation and metadata retrieval.\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 15,\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"STORY-setup-005\"\n      ],\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"STORY-storage-002\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement Upload Intent API Endpoint with Media Validation\",\n      \"description\": \"Create backend endpoint POST /api/v1/storage/upload-intent to validate file metadata against audio and image size/MIME rules before returning direct-to-storage presigned upload URLs.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"Endpoint accepts fileType ('audio'|'image'), fileName, fileSizeBytes, and mimeType.\",\n        \"Audio uploads are restricted to MP3 (audio/mpeg) and WAV (audio/wav) up to 50MB (52,428,800 bytes) per constraint 1.\",\n        \"Cover image uploads are restricted to JPEG, PNG, and WebP up to 10MB (10,485,760 bytes).\",\n        \"Invalid file formats or sizes exceeding limits return HTTP 422 Unprocessable Entity with details before presigning.\",\n        \"Valid requests return HTTP 200 OK with a 60-minute presigned PUT URL and deterministic object key (audio/{artistId}/{trackId}_{uuid}.{ext} or images/{artistId}/{imageId}_{uuid}.webp).\",\n        \"Integration test verifies POST /api/v1/storage/upload-intent with valid and invalid audio payloads.\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 16,\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"STORY-storage-001\",\n        \"STORY-security-005\"\n      ],\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"STORY-storage-003\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement Presigned Playback Stream URL Endpoint and Byte Range Headers\",\n      \"description\": \"Create backend endpoint GET /api/v1/tracks/:id/stream to issue short-lived GET presigned playback URLs (15-minute TTL) with HTTP byte-range request header support for low-latency streaming.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"Request generates a presigned GET URL with a 900-second (15-minute) expiration for track playback per DEC-008.\",\n        \"Allows unauthenticated guest access for public track streaming per DEC-005.\",\n        \"Emits HTTP response headers Accept-Ranges: bytes and Cache-Control: private, max-age=900.\",\n        \"Supports HTTP 206 Partial Content range responses with Content-Range: bytes <start>-<end>/<total> to meet SLA of under 2 seconds audio playback start per sec-024.\",\n        \"Unit tests verify stream URL generation and expiry configuration.\",\n        \"Integration test calls GET /api/v1/tracks/:id/stream and verifies response headers and presigned stream URL payload.\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 17,\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"STORY-storage-001\",\n        \"STORY-setup-004\"\n      ],\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"STORY-storage-004\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement Frontend Direct-to-Storage Upload Hook and Upload Component\",\n      \"description\": \"Build React hook useDirectUpload and UI component FileUploadProgress to request presigned upload URLs from the storage API and execute client-side direct binary uploads to S3/R2 with progress indicators.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"useDirectUpload hook manages request flow: POST /upload-intent, direct S3/R2 PUT binary transfer, progress state, and completion.\",\n        \"UI displays real-time progress bar, transfer percentage, and error notifications adhering to design tokens.\",\n        \"Pre-upload client validation checks file size (max 50MB audio) and MIME format before network requests.\",\n        \"Upload controls and progress indicators satisfy WCAG 2.1 AA accessibility keyboard and screen reader standards per constraint 5.\",\n        \"Responsive layout scales down gracefully to 375px mobile viewports per sec-026.\",\n        \"Unit tests in tests/unit/components/upload.test.tsx test hook states and upload validation.\",\n        \"Playwright E2E spec in e2e/tests/upload-flow.spec.ts verifies selecting an audio file, observing progress, and completing direct upload.\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 18,\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"STORY-storage-002\",\n        \"STORY-setup-003\"\n      ],\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"STORY-auth-001\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement User Registration API Endpoint and Payload Validation\",\n      \"description\": \"Build POST /api/v1/auth/register API endpoint to validate registration payloads, enforce email normalization and uniqueness, create User records with bcrypt password hashes, and return a 7-day session cookie.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"Accepts { email, password, displayName }, normalizes email to lowercase, and validates password strength (min 8 chars, 1 uppercase, 1 lowercase, 1 digit).\",\n        \"Returns HTTP 409 Conflict with code AUTH_EMAIL_EXISTS if email is already registered.\",\n        \"Hashes password using bcrypt cost 12 and creates User record with role LISTENER per DEC-004.\",\n        \"Sets __Host-indie_session HTTP-only, SameSite=Strict cookie with 7-day TTL and returns HTTP 201 Created with sanitized user object.\",\n        \"Timestamps (createdAt) are stored and returned in UTC ISO-8601 format per constraint 0.\",\n        \"Passwords are sanitized out of response payloads and never logged per constraint 4 and sec-024 rules.\",\n        \"Integration test asserts POST /api/v1/auth/register creates user, sets session cookie, and returns sanitized envelope.\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 19,\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"STORY-security-001\",\n        \"STORY-security-002\",\n        \"STORY-setup-004\"\n      ],\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"STORY-auth-002\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement User Login API Endpoint with Rate Limiting\",\n      \"description\": \"Build POST /api/v1/auth/login endpoint to authenticate registered users via email and password, issue session cookies, and enforce a 5-attempt per 15-minute rate limit policy per IP address.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"Validates email and password, returning HTTP 200 OK and setting the 7-day __Host-indie_session cookie upon successful match.\",\n        \"Returns HTTP 401 Unauthorized with code INVALID_CREDENTIALS for non-existent emails or incorrect passwords.\",\n        \"Enforces rate limiting: exceeding 5 failed login attempts in 15 minutes per IP triggers HTTP 429 Too Many Requests with code RATE_LIMIT_EXCEEDED per sec-025.\",\n        \"Password inputs and failure attempts do not output plaintext credentials to application loggers per constraint 4.\",\n        \"Integration test verifies successful login cookie issuance, 401 error envelope on invalid credentials, and 429 rate limit triggering after 5 failed attempts.\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 20,\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"STORY-security-001\",\n        \"STORY-security-002\"\n      ],\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"STORY-auth-003\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement Password Reset and Credential Management APIs\",\n      \"description\": \"Implement backend endpoints POST /api/v1/auth/forgot-password, POST /api/v1/auth/reset-password, and PATCH /api/v1/auth/password for self-service password recovery and authenticated credential updates.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"POST /api/v1/auth/forgot-password generates a 60-minute reset token stored as a hash in DB and returns a uniform HTTP 200 OK response to prevent email enumeration.\",\n        \"POST /api/v1/auth/reset-password validates reset token, updates bcrypt password hash, invalidates used token, and revokes active session cookies.\",\n        \"PATCH /api/v1/auth/password verifies caller's currentPassword, updates to newPassword, and regenerates the session token.\",\n        \"Password reset tokens and updated hashes use UTC ISO-8601 expiration timestamps per constraint 0.\",\n        \"Integration tests cover forgot password uniform response, reset password execution, token expiry rejection, and credential update logic.\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 21,\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"STORY-auth-001\",\n        \"STORY-security-001\"\n      ],\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"STORY-auth-004\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement Log Sanitization and Password Field Protection Middleware\",\n      \"description\": \"Build global logging middleware to intercept incoming request bodies on auth routes and sanitize sensitive credential fields (password, oldPassword, newPassword) before passing logs to central monitoring.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"Middleware inspects incoming payload bodies on /api/v1/auth/* routes and replaces sensitive keys with [REDACTED].\",\n        \"Structured application error logs strip password fields from stack traces and error details.\",\n        \"Data in transit is enforced over TLS 1.3 encrypted connections per sec-025.\",\n        \"Unit tests in tests/unit/middleware/sanitizer.test.ts verify payload redaction across various nested JSON structures.\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 22,\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"STORY-setup-006\",\n        \"STORY-security-001\"\n      ],\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"effort\": \"small\",\n      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"STORY-auth-005\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement Guest Session Migration Service\",\n      \"description\": \"Create client and backend helper functions to migrate temporary in-memory/localStorage guest playlist drafts and queue state into permanent Playlist records upon user registration or sign-in.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"Guest session state reader extracts local draft playlist tracks from client storage post-registration.\",\n        \"Client issues POST /api/v1/playlists with guest playlist data to create permanent database records linked to the new User.id.\",\n        \"Active audio streaming player state is preserved continuously across registration without resetting playback per DEC-005.\",\n        \"Unit tests verify guest state extraction and payload formatting.\",\n        \"Integration test validates converting a guest playlist payload into a persisted Playlist entity.\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 23,\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"STORY-auth-001\",\n        \"STORY-setup-004\"\n      ],\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"STORY-auth-006\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement Frontend Account Registration Page and Interactive Form\",\n      \"description\": \"Build Next.js user registration page /register featuring Zod schema client-side validation, password strength meter, show/hide password toggle, accessible loading states, and responsive shadcn layout.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"Renders /register page using dark-mode design system tokens, responsive grid layouts down to 375px mobile viewports per sec-026.\",\n        \"Input fields for email, password, and displayName validate on blur and submit using Zod schema rules.\",\n        \"Password input features an interactive visibility toggle button (masked vs unmasked) and real-time password strength meter.\",\n        \"API submission displays active loading spinner on submit button, disables re-clicks with aria-disabled=\\\"true\\\".\",\n        \"Server errors (such as AUTH_EMAIL_EXISTS) render in an accessible alert banner at the top of the form with focus moved to the first invalid field per WCAG 2.1 AA (constraint 5).\",\n        \"Unit tests verify form validation rules and component state transitions.\",\n        \"Playwright E2E spec e2e/tests/register.spec.ts covers successful registration, duplicate email handling, and validation error display.\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 24,\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"STORY-auth-001\",\n        \"STORY-setup-003\"\n      ],\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"STORY-auth-007\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement Frontend Login Page and Form Component\",\n      \"description\": \"Build Next.js user login page /login with Zod validation, error callout banners, password visibility toggle, guest session migration trigger, and seamless redirect after authentication.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"Renders /login page using design tokens and responsive layout down to 375px mobile viewport per sec-026.\",\n        \"Form validates email and password inputs, displaying inline feedback on invalid submission.\",\n        \"Successful login triggers guest session state migration if guest playlist items exist in local storage per DEC-005.\",\n        \"Password field includes show/hide visibility toggle and accessible label associations complying with WCAG 2.1 AA per constraint 5.\",\n        \"Server authentication errors (such as INVALID_CREDENTIALS or RATE_LIMIT_EXCEEDED) display in an accessible alert callout banner.\",\n        \"Unit tests verify login form states and submit event handling.\",\n        \"Playwright E2E spec e2e/tests/login.spec.ts tests valid login flow, invalid credentials error, and guest migration trigger.\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 25,\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"STORY-auth-002\",\n        \"STORY-auth-005\",\n        \"STORY-setup-003\"\n      ],\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"STORY-auth-008\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement Frontend Password Recovery Pages\",\n      \"description\": \"Build Next.js UI pages /forgot-password and /reset-password allowing users to request password reset links and submit new credentials with real-time feedback and accessibility.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"/forgot-password page accepts email and presents a confirmation message regardless of email existence to prevent account enumeration.\",\n        \"/reset-password page extracts reset token from URL query params and validates new password against strength rules before submitting.\",\n        \"Visual feedback banners notify user of successful password reset and provide a link to sign in.\",\n        \"Form controls adhere to WCAG 2.1 AA keyboard navigation and screen reader standards per constraint 5.\",\n        \"Unit tests verify form schema validation and token state handling.\",\n        \"Playwright E2E spec e2e/tests/password-reset.spec.ts verifies full password recovery user flow from forgot-password submission to reset-password update.\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 26,\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"STORY-auth-003\",\n        \"STORY-setup-003\"\n      ],\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"STORY-role-001\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement Listener to Artist Role Upgrade API Endpoint\",\n      \"description\": \"Create the POST /api/v1/users/me/upgrade-to-artist API endpoint allowing registered Listener users to upgrade to an Artist role. Executes an atomic transaction to append the ARTIST role flag to User.roles, provision a linked ArtistProfile model, and return an updated JWT session payload. Preserves existing user favorites, playlists, and follow relationships without requiring re-registration.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"POST /api/v1/users/me/upgrade-to-artist appends 'ARTIST' to User.roles while preserving 'LISTENER' privileges.\",\n        \"Provisions an ArtistProfile record with userId, stageName (defaulting to User.name if omitted), bio, genreTags, and initial followerCount=0, trackCount=0.\",\n        \"Returns HTTP 200 OK with the updated User object, new ArtistProfile, and a fresh JWT containing revised role claims.\",\n        \"Timestamps in the response payload are formatted in UTC ISO-8601 per constraint [0].\",\n        \"Unit tests in src/services/role.test.ts verify atomic role update and default stageName fallback logic.\",\n        \"Integration test calls POST /api/v1/users/me/upgrade-to-artist with valid payload and asserts HTTP 200 plus correct database state.\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 27,\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"STORY-setup-004\",\n        \"STORY-security-002\"\n      ],\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"STORY-role-002\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement Verification Email Generation and Dispatch Service\",\n      \"description\": \"Build the backend service and API endpoint POST /api/v1/auth/verify-email/request to generate cryptographically secure email verification tokens. Generates a 64-character hex token via crypto.randomBytes(32), stores a SHA-256 digest in the database with a 24-hour expiration window, invalidates previous active tokens, and dispatches a single-use verification link via email.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"POST /api/v1/auth/verify-email/request generates a 64-character random token and persists its SHA-256 digest with expiresAt set 24 hours in the future.\",\n        \"Invalidates any existing active verification token records for the requesting user prior to creating a new token.\",\n        \"Returns HTTP 202 Accepted with a confirmation message and expiresInSeconds=86400.\",\n        \"Applies rate limiting on POST /api/v1/auth/verify-email/request per cross-cutting security policy sec-025.\",\n        \"Unit tests in src/services/emailVerification.test.ts cover token generation, SHA-256 hashing, and prior token invalidation.\",\n        \"Integration test calls POST /api/v1/auth/verify-email/request for an authenticated user and asserts HTTP 202 status and DB record.\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 28,\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"STORY-setup-004\",\n        \"STORY-security-002\"\n      ],\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"STORY-role-003\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement Email Verification Token Confirmation and Status APIs\",\n      \"description\": \"Implement POST /api/v1/auth/verify-email/confirm to validate incoming raw tokens against SHA-256 database digests and GET /api/v1/users/me/verification-status to retrieve email verification status. Validates token freshness (expiresAt > current_time), sets User.emailVerified to true with a UTC ISO-8601 timestamp, deletes used token records, and returns explicit status data.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"POST /api/v1/auth/verify-email/confirm hashes incoming raw token with SHA-256 and matches against active database records.\",\n        \"If token is valid and unexpired, updates User.emailVerified to true, sets emailVerifiedAt to UTC ISO-8601 timestamp, and deletes the token record.\",\n        \"If token is invalid or expired, returns HTTP 400 Bad Request with error code INVALID_VERIFICATION_TOKEN.\",\n        \"GET /api/v1/users/me/verification-status returns HTTP 200 OK with emailVerified, canUpload boolean, and roles array.\",\n        \"Unit tests in src/services/emailVerificationConfirm.test.ts cover valid token processing, expired token rejection, and invalid digest matching.\",\n        \"Integration test calls POST /api/v1/auth/verify-email/confirm with valid and invalid tokens and verifies exact HTTP responses.\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 29,\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"STORY-role-002\"\n      ],\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"STORY-role-004\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement Email Verification Gating Middleware for Track Uploads\",\n      \"description\": \"Implement the requireVerifiedEmail middleware enforcing DEC-004, which restricts track upload execution exclusively to users with verified email addresses. Intercepts request flows targeting POST /api/v1/tracks and POST /api/v1/tracks/upload-intent, rejecting unverified users with HTTP 403 Forbidden without affecting streaming, search, or playlist actions.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"requireVerifiedEmail middleware checks User.emailVerified property on authenticated request contexts.\",\n        \"If User.emailVerified is false, rejects request immediately with HTTP 403 Forbidden and code EMAIL_NOT_VERIFIED containing resendUrl.\",\n        \"Allows verified users with ARTIST role to proceed through upload execution handlers.\",\n        \"Explicitly leaves streaming, playback, search, following, and playlist endpoints ungated per DEC-004 and DEC-005.\",\n        \"Unit tests in src/middleware/requireVerifiedEmail.test.ts verify passthrough for verified users and rejection for unverified accounts.\",\n        \"Integration test verifies that POST /api/v1/tracks returns 403 when invoked by an unverified account.\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 30,\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"STORY-role-003\",\n        \"STORY-security-005\"\n      ],\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"effort\": \"small\",\n      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"STORY-role-005\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement Frontend Artist Upgrade Form and Settings Section\",\n      \"description\": \"Build the frontend artist role upgrade modal and account settings form component allowing Listeners to transition into Artists. Collects stageName, bio, and genreTags with client-side validation, submits data to POST /api/v1/users/me/upgrade-to-artist, updates global authentication state, and displays creator onboarding guidance.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"Renders form fields for stageName (1-50 chars), bio (max 500 chars), and genreTags (1-5 tags select) within account settings.\",\n        \"Complies with WCAG 2.1 AA keyboard accessibility standards and visible focus highlights per constraint [5].\",\n        \"On successful submission, updates session context with ARTIST role and redirects or shows artist dashboard link without requiring re-login.\",\n        \"Displays error alert banner if validation or API failure occurs.\",\n        \"Unit tests in src/components/ArtistUpgradeForm.test.tsx verify field validation, submission handling, and accessibility attributes.\",\n        \"Playwright spec in e2e/tests/artist-upgrade.spec.ts covers filling out the upgrade form, submitting, and verifying updated role state.\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 31,\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"STORY-role-001\",\n        \"STORY-setup-003\"\n      ],\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"STORY-role-006\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement Frontend Email Verification Confirmation Page and Notification Banner\",\n      \"description\": \"Construct the email verification landing page (/verify-email) and sticky notification banner for unverified creator accounts. Reads the token query parameter on mount, invokes POST /api/v1/auth/verify-email/confirm, renders success or error confirmation states, and provides a one-click resend button triggering POST /api/v1/auth/verify-email/request.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"Landing page at /verify-email extracts token parameter and automatically triggers confirmation API request on load.\",\n        \"Renders success message with button to return to artist dashboard upon HTTP 200 OK response.\",\n        \"Renders error alert with explicit message and 'Resend Verification Email' action button when token is invalid or expired.\",\n        \"Displays a persistent banner in creator views when User.emailVerified is false, explaining upload gating per DEC-004.\",\n        \"Unit tests in src/pages/VerifyEmail.test.tsx verify token extraction, API invocation states, and error handling UI.\",\n        \"Playwright spec in e2e/tests/email-verification.spec.ts tests visiting /verify-email with valid and expired tokens.\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 32,\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"STORY-role-003\",\n        \"STORY-setup-003\"\n      ],\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"STORY-profile-001\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement Get Public Artist Profile API with Aggregated Metrics\",\n      \"description\": \"Develop the GET /api/v1/artists/:artistId endpoint to fetch public artist profiles, live tracks, and real-time aggregated metrics. Aggregates total plays across live tracks, total likes count, and followers count, and includes top 5 popular tracks ordered descending by play count.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"GET /api/v1/artists/:artistId returns public profile details (displayName, bio, avatarUrl, headerImageUrl, socialLinks, isVerified).\",\n        \"Calculates and returns aggregated stats: totalPlays (sum of live track playCounts), totalLikes (count of likes across tracks), and followerCount.\",\n        \"Returns top 5 tracks owned by artist with status 'LIVE' ordered descending by playCount.\",\n        \"Accessible to unauthenticated guest users per DEC-005, returning isFollowing boolean if authenticated request context exists.\",\n        \"Unit tests in src/services/artistProfile.test.ts cover aggregation calculations, popular track selection, and guest request handling.\",\n        \"Integration test calls GET /api/v1/artists/:artistId and verifies response schema, stats accuracy, and 200 HTTP status.\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 33,\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"STORY-role-001\",\n        \"STORY-setup-008\"\n      ],\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"STORY-profile-002\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement Update Artist Profile API Endpoint and Payload Validation\",\n      \"description\": \"Create the PATCH /api/v1/artist-profile API endpoint allowing creators with the ARTIST role to update branding metadata. Validates payload fields against strict schema constraints (displayName 1-50 chars, bio max 500 chars, socialLinks max 5 HTTPS entries) and returns 422 error codes upon validation failure.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"PATCH /api/v1/artist-profile enforces ARTIST role authorization requirement.\",\n        \"Validates displayName (1-50 chars, trimmed), bio (max 500 chars), and socialLinks (max 5 items, valid HTTPS URLs with matching platforms).\",\n        \"Returns HTTP 422 Unprocessable Entity with codes INVALID_DISPLAY_NAME, BIO_TOO_LONG, or INVALID_SOCIAL_LINKS upon invalid payloads.\",\n        \"Returns HTTP 200 OK with the updated ArtistProfile payload upon successful modification.\",\n        \"Unit tests in src/validators/artistProfile.test.ts verify field validation rules and error payload generation.\",\n        \"Integration test executes PATCH /api/v1/artist-profile with valid and invalid payloads and verifies responses.\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 34,\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"STORY-role-001\",\n        \"STORY-security-005\"\n      ],\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"STORY-profile-003\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement Avatar and Header Image Upload Endpoints for Artist Profiles\",\n      \"description\": \"Build the POST /api/v1/artist-profile/avatar and POST /api/v1/artist-profile/header endpoints for multipart image uploads. Validates image file sizes (max 5MB), MIME types (JPEG, PNG, WebP), uploads assets to cloud storage via StorageProvider, and updates avatarUrl or headerImageUrl on the ArtistProfile model.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"POST /api/v1/artist-profile/avatar and /header endpoints accept multipart image file uploads up to 5MB.\",\n        \"Validates MIME type to ensure file is image/jpeg, image/png, or image/webp, returning 422 INVALID_AVATAR_URL or INVALID_HEADER_URL on mismatch.\",\n        \"Uploads processed images to storage provider and updates target ArtistProfile record with HTTPS asset URL.\",\n        \"Requires ARTIST role authorization and returns updated profile payload in JSON envelope.\",\n        \"Unit tests in src/services/profileImageUpload.test.ts cover file type validation, size checking, and storage provider invocation.\",\n        \"Integration test posts image files to avatar/header endpoints and asserts HTTP 200 status and updated profile fields.\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 35,\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"STORY-profile-002\",\n        \"STORY-storage-001\"\n      ],\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"STORY-profile-004\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement Listener Public Profile API Endpoint\",\n      \"description\": \"Develop the GET /api/v1/users/:userId endpoint for fetching public listener profiles. Returns basic user metadata (username, avatar, registration year), public playlists grid data (where isPublic=true), and a list of followed artists.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"GET /api/v1/users/:userId returns public user info including username, avatarUrl, and createdAt registration year.\",\n        \"Includes public playlists list created by the user where isPublic is true, formatted with title, trackCount, and cover mosaic.\",\n        \"Includes array of followed ArtistProfile summary objects.\",\n        \"Accessible to both authenticated users and unauthenticated guests per DEC-005.\",\n        \"Unit tests in src/services/listenerProfile.test.ts verify filtering of private playlists and proper profile serialization.\",\n        \"Integration test calls GET /api/v1/users/:userId and asserts HTTP 200 response with correct public data.\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 36,\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"STORY-setup-008\"\n      ],\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"STORY-profile-005\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement Account Suspension and Banned Status Profile Isolation Filter\",\n      \"description\": \"Implement global security filtering to soft-hide suspended or banned profiles and content per DEC-003. Ensures GET /api/v1/artists/:artistId and GET /api/v1/users/:userId return HTTP 404 Not Found when target accounts are suspended or banned, filtering them out of public searches and catalog queries.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"If a target User record has status 'SUSPENDED' or 'BANNED', profile endpoints GET /api/v1/artists/:artistId and GET /api/v1/users/:userId return HTTP 404 NOT_FOUND.\",\n        \"Filters out suspended or banned artists and their tracks from search indices and catalog listing queries.\",\n        \"Maintains database record integrity without hard-deleting underlying tracks or profiles per DEC-003.\",\n        \"Unit tests in src/middleware/statusIsolation.test.ts cover profile 404 responses for suspended and banned user states.\",\n        \"Integration test verifies that querying a suspended artist's profile route returns a standardized 404 error envelope.\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 37,\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"STORY-profile-001\",\n        \"STORY-profile-004\"\n      ],\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"effort\": \"small\",\n      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"STORY-profile-006\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement Frontend Public Artist Profile Page and Discography View\",\n      \"description\": \"Construct the public artist profile view (/artists/[artistId]) displaying branding header, metrics bar, popular tracks section, and paginated discography. Renders dynamic header banner, circular avatar, follower count, follow/unfollow toggle, popular tracks table (top 5), and full track catalog with sorting options.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"Renders header banner image (16:9 ratio with default gradient fallback), 128x128px circular avatar, displayName, bio, and social links.\",\n        \"Displays metrics bar showing formatted total plays, total likes, and follower counts using compact notation (e.g. 1.2K).\",\n        \"Renders Popular Tracks section (up to 5 items) with inline play buttons, genre badges, duration, and play/like counts.\",\n        \"Displays full published track catalog with Release Date (default) and Title sort controls, supporting infinite scroll loading.\",\n        \"Includes interactive Follow/Unfollow button that toggles state for logged-in users and prompts login modal for guests.\",\n        \"Unit tests in src/pages/ArtistProfileView.test.tsx cover header rendering, stats formatting, track list sorting, and follow button interaction.\",\n        \"Playwright spec in e2e/tests/artist-profile.spec.ts verifies visiting /artists/[artistId], interacting with play triggers, and sorting discography.\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 38,\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"STORY-profile-001\",\n        \"STORY-setup-003\"\n      ],\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"effort\": \"high\",\n      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"STORY-profile-007\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement Frontend Artist Profile Management and Image Upload Dashboard\",\n      \"description\": \"Build the artist profile editing dashboard UI allowing creators to update stage name, bio, social links, and upload avatar/header banner images. Features drag-and-drop file uploaders with image preview cropped ratios, real-time character counters, and inline validation error messages.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"Provides form controls for editing stageName, bio (with 500-char counter), and up to 5 social links with platform selectors.\",\n        \"Includes file input uploaders for avatar (1:1 crop preview) and header banner (16:9 crop preview) with 5MB file size validation.\",\n        \"Submits image uploads to /api/v1/artist-profile/avatar and /header and metadata changes to PATCH /api/v1/artist-profile.\",\n        \"Displays toast notifications on successful save or inline error alerts on 422 response validation failures.\",\n        \"Unit tests in src/components/ArtistProfileEditor.test.tsx test preview generation, char counter math, and form submission.\",\n        \"Playwright spec in e2e/tests/artist-profile-edit.spec.ts covers modifying bio text, selecting avatar image, and saving profile changes.\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 39,\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"STORY-profile-002\",\n        \"STORY-profile-003\",\n        \"STORY-setup-003\"\n      ],\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"STORY-profile-008\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement Frontend Public Listener Profile Page\",\n      \"description\": \"Construct the public listener profile page (/users/[userId]) displaying user avatar, registration year, public playlists grid, and followed artists carousel. Renders public playlist cards showing cover mosaics and track counts, alongside a horizontal slider of followed artists.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"Renders header section with user avatar, username, and registration year.\",\n        \"Displays Public Playlists Grid showing cards for playlists where isPublic is true, featuring cover art mosaic, title, and track count.\",\n        \"Renders Followed Artists Carousel allowing horizontal scroll through followed creator cards.\",\n        \"Complies with WCAG 2.1 AA keyboard accessibility and responsive layout guidelines down to 375px viewports per constraint [5].\",\n        \"Unit tests in src/pages/ListenerProfileView.test.tsx verify playlist grid rendering and followed artists carousel structure.\",\n        \"Playwright spec in e2e/tests/listener-profile.spec.ts tests loading a listener profile page and clicking a public playlist card.\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 40,\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"STORY-profile-004\",\n        \"STORY-setup-003\"\n      ],\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"STORY-track-001\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement Track Upload Intent API Endpoint with Presigned URL Generation\",\n      \"description\": \"Develop the POST /api/v1/tracks/upload-intent endpoint validating media file parameters and issuing direct-to-storage presigned PUT URLs per DEC-008. Validates audio size (max 50MB per constraint [1]), audio MIME type (audio/mpeg, audio/wav), cover size (max 5MB), and returns short-lived S3/R2 presigned upload tokens.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"POST /api/v1/tracks/upload-intent checks requireVerifiedEmail gating rule and ARTIST role context.\",\n        \"Enforces max 50MB (52,428,800 bytes) audio file limit and audio/mpeg or audio/wav MIME types per constraint [1].\",\n        \"Enforces max 5MB cover image limit and image/jpeg, image/png, or image/webp MIME types.\",\n        \"Returns HTTP 200 OK with audioUploadUrl (15-min presigned PUT URL), audioStorageKey, optional coverImageUploadUrl/Key, and UTC ISO-8601 expiresAt timestamp.\",\n        \"Unit tests in src/services/uploadIntent.test.ts verify MIME type validation, file size checks, and presigned URL parameters.\",\n        \"Integration test calls POST /api/v1/tracks/upload-intent with valid payload and asserts response key formats and 200 status.\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 41,\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"STORY-role-004\",\n        \"STORY-storage-002\"\n      ],\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"STORY-track-002\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement Server-Side Audio Metadata Extraction and Binary Header Inspection Service\",\n      \"description\": \"Build an out-of-band audio processing service that inspects uploaded binary audio streams in storage to extract metadata. Reads headers to verify codec integrity, channel count, sample rate, bitrate, and precise duration in float seconds, detecting corrupted or spoofed audio files.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"Service connects via StorageProvider interface to read initial audio binary header bytes from storage.\",\n        \"Extracts precise track duration in float seconds (e.g. 218.42), bitrate, sample rate, and channel topology.\",\n        \"Verifies container format matches declared MIME type (MP3 or WAV per constraint [1]).\",\n        \"Throws a typed CorruptedAudioError if the file header is unparseable, incomplete, or corrupted.\",\n        \"Unit tests in src/services/audioMetadata.test.ts cover valid MP3/WAV header parsing and corrupted file detection.\",\n        \"Integration test executes metadata extraction against sample audio files in local test storage.\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 42,\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"STORY-storage-001\"\n      ],\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"STORY-track-003\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement Track Registration API Endpoint with Auto-Live Status and Cover Image Linking\",\n      \"description\": \"Create the POST /api/v1/tracks registration endpoint to finalize track publishing. Invokes the audio metadata extraction service, sets status to LIVE per auto-live decision DEC-001, assigns cover art (or fallback genre default), persists the Track document in MongoDB via Prisma, and returns the track payload.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"POST /api/v1/tracks validates title (1-100 chars), genre (normalized taxonomy), and audioStorageKey presence.\",\n        \"Triggers out-of-band audio duration extraction and stores floating-point seconds on Track.duration.\",\n        \"Sets Track.status to 'LIVE' automatically per DEC-001 without requiring pre-upload admin approval.\",\n        \"Links provided coverImageStorageKey or assigns default genre cover URL /static/covers/defaults/{genre}.png if omitted.\",\n        \"Returns HTTP 201 Created with full Track object containing UTC ISO-8601 timestamps per constraint [0].\",\n        \"Unit tests in src/services/trackRegistration.test.ts verify auto-live assignment, default cover art fallback, and metadata persistence.\",\n        \"Integration test calls POST /api/v1/tracks with valid keys and asserts 201 status and DB Track record.\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 43,\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"STORY-track-001\",\n        \"STORY-track-002\"\n      ],\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"STORY-track-004\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement Genre Tagging Validation and Search Indexing Trigger Service\",\n      \"description\": \"Implement genre validation against the normalized platform taxonomy (INDIE_ROCK, BEDROOM_POP, ELECTRONIC, HIP_HOP, LO_FI, AMBIENT, R_AND_B, FOLK, OTHER) and event dispatching for search indexing. Triggers background search index updates and genre queue aggregation upon track creation.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"Validates genre field against platform taxonomy enum values, rejecting invalid genres with 422 INVALID_GENRE_TAG.\",\n        \"Dispatches post-creation background event to index new track title, artist stageName, and genre in search layer.\",\n        \"Appends new track ID to the rule-based genre recommendation queue upon database insertion.\",\n        \"Unit tests in src/services/genreIndexing.test.ts cover taxonomy validation and indexing event payload creation.\",\n        \"Integration test verifies that creating a track fires the expected search indexing event trigger.\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 44,\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"STORY-track-003\"\n      ],\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"effort\": \"small\",\n      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"STORY-track-005\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement Storage Cleanup and Error Recovery Handlers for Upload Failures\",\n      \"description\": \"Develop error recovery workflows for corrupt audio files or failed registration payloads. If audio header parsing fails or validation errors occur during track registration, executes automatic StorageProvider.deleteObject calls for orphan storage keys and returns HTTP 422 CORRUPTED_AUDIO_FILE.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"If audio metadata extraction fails or header is corrupted, invokes StorageProvider.deleteObject on audioStorageKey and coverImageStorageKey.\",\n        \"Returns HTTP 422 Unprocessable Entity with error code CORRUPTED_AUDIO_FILE.\",\n        \"Handles missing storage key errors during registration by returning HTTP 404 STORAGE_KEY_NOT_FOUND.\",\n        \"Logs failure events with sanitized PII metadata for monitoring per cross-cutting guidelines sec-025.\",\n        \"Unit tests in src/services/uploadErrorRecovery.test.ts verify storage deletion invocation and error envelope generation.\",\n        \"Integration test simulates corrupted file header and verifies storage cleanup execution and 422 response.\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 45,\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"STORY-track-003\",\n        \"STORY-storage-001\"\n      ],\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"STORY-track-006\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement Frontend Track Upload Page and Interactive Multi-Step Upload Form\",\n      \"description\": \"Construct the frontend creator track upload page (/dashboard/upload) featuring file drag-and-drop pickers, direct presigned S3/R2 upload execution with real-time percentage progress bar, metadata entry form (title, genre, description, cover image), and auto-live success redirect.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"Renders drag-and-drop file upload zone enforcing client-side max 50MB size and MP3/WAV format checks per constraint [1].\",\n        \"Executes two-step upload flow: calls /upload-intent API, issues direct PUT request to presigned URL with visual progress bar, then submits metadata to /api/v1/tracks.\",\n        \"Provides form inputs for track title (1-100 chars), genre dropdown (platform taxonomy), description (max 500 chars), and cover art image picker.\",\n        \"Complies with WCAG 2.1 AA accessibility guidelines with aria-valuenow on progress bars and screen reader status updates per constraint [5].\",\n        \"Displays clear error banner and retry action if upload or metadata processing fails.\",\n        \"Unit tests in src/components/TrackUploadWizard.test.tsx test file drag-and-drop validation, upload progress calculation, and form submission.\",\n        \"Playwright spec in e2e/tests/track-upload.spec.ts tests picking an MP3 file, filling metadata, uploading, and verifying redirect to published track view.\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 46,\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"STORY-track-001\",\n        \"STORY-track-003\",\n        \"STORY-storage-004\",\n        \"STORY-setup-003\"\n      ],\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"effort\": \"high\",\n      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"STORY-track-007\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement Track Metadata Update API Endpoint and Payload Validation\",\n      \"description\": \"Create the REST API endpoint PATCH /api/v1/tracks/[id] allowing Artists and Admins to modify track title, coverImageUrl, and genre tag. Enforce server-side identity and ownership verification, validate payload fields, reject immutable field edit attempts with HTTP 422 IMMUTABLE_FIELD_REJECTED, and trigger tag-based cache revalidation.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"PATCH /api/v1/tracks/[id] requires authentication and Artist or Admin role, returning 403 ARTIST_PROFILE_REQUIRED if requesting user has no associated ArtistProfile.\",\n        \"Server compares Track.artistProfileId against user's ArtistProfile.id, returning HTTP 403 Forbidden with code FORBIDDEN_OWNERSHIP_MISMATCH if mismatched and user is not Admin.\",\n        \"Payload validation accepts optional title (1-100 characters, trimmed), coverImageUrl (valid HTTP/S URL under 5MB), and genre (matching allowed system genre taxonomy).\",\n        \"Including any immutable field (audioUrl, duration, playCount, likeCount, artistProfileId) in the request body triggers HTTP 422 Unprocessable Entity with code IMMUTABLE_FIELD_REJECTED.\",\n        \"Successful metadata updates mutate database record, set updatedAt in UTC ISO-8601 format, revalidate cache tags (track-[id], artist-catalog-[artistProfileId], genre-feed-[genre]), and return 200 OK with updated metadata.\",\n        \"Admin-initiated metadata edits emit an immutable entry to AuditLog capturing admin user ID, track ID, and modified fields.\",\n        \"Integration tests in tests/api/track-update.test.ts call PATCH /api/v1/tracks/[id] with valid owner payload (asserts 200), immutable payload (asserts 422), unauthorized user (asserts 403), and non-existent track (asserts 404).\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 47,\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"STORY-setup-006\",\n        \"STORY-track-003\",\n        \"STORY-security-005\"\n      ],\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"STORY-track-008\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement Asynchronous Storage Cleanup for Replaced Track Cover Art\",\n      \"description\": \"Create an asynchronous storage cleanup background job triggered when a track's coverImageUrl is updated via PATCH /api/v1/tracks/[id]. Extract the previous cover image key and execute StorageProvider.deleteFile() out-of-band to prevent storage waste.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"When PATCH /api/v1/tracks/[id] updates coverImageUrl to a new URL, the handler enqueues a background task with the previous cover art storage key.\",\n        \"Asynchronous job invokes StorageProvider.deleteFile(key) to permanently delete the orphaned cover image asset from object storage (S3/R2).\",\n        \"If coverImageUrl is omitted or unchanged in the update payload, no storage deletion job is enqueued.\",\n        \"Storage provider deletion failures are logged as structured errors and retried without blocking or failing the HTTP PATCH response.\",\n        \"Unit tests in tests/unit/cover-art-cleanup.test.ts verify that StorageProvider.deleteFile() is called with the exact previous key when coverImageUrl changes.\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 48,\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"STORY-track-007\",\n        \"STORY-storage-001\"\n      ],\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"effort\": \"small\",\n      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"STORY-track-009\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement Track Soft Archival Deletion Endpoint and Stream Interceptor\",\n      \"description\": \"Create the DELETE /api/v1/tracks/[id] endpoint to soft-delete tracks by setting deletedAt to the current UTC ISO-8601 timestamp and status to archived. Update streaming route handlers to intercept requests for soft-deleted tracks and return HTTP 404 TRACK_ARCHIVED.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"DELETE /api/v1/tracks/[id] requires authentication and ownership verification (or Admin role), returning 403 FORBIDDEN_OWNERSHIP_MISMATCH on mismatch.\",\n        \"Successful deletion updates Track.deletedAt to current UTC ISO-8601 timestamp and sets Track.status to archived.\",\n        \"Global data access queries enforce mandatory filter deletedAt: null, instantly hiding soft-deleted tracks from search, feeds, recommendations, artist profiles, and follower activity feeds.\",\n        \"GET /api/v1/tracks/[id]/stream checks deletedAt !== null or status === 'archived' and returns HTTP 404 with structured error body { \\\"error\\\": { \\\"code\\\": \\\"TRACK_ARCHIVED\\\", \\\"message\\\": \\\"This track is no longer available.\\\" } }.\",\n        \"Admin track soft-deletion emits an entry to AuditLog capturing admin ID, track ID, and timestamp.\",\n        \"Integration tests in tests/api/track-delete.test.ts verify soft-archival database state, 404 response on streaming archived track, and 403 on unauthorized deletion.\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 49,\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"STORY-setup-006\",\n        \"STORY-track-007\",\n        \"STORY-storage-003\"\n      ],\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"STORY-track-010\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement Synchronous Playlist Cascade Cleanup and Catalog Counter Sync\",\n      \"description\": \"Create a synchronous database cascade cleanup service executed during track soft-deletion. Purge all PlaylistTrack junction records referencing the track, re-index position ordering for remaining playlist items, decrement playlist track counts, and decrement artist total track count.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"Triggered synchronously within single database transaction during DELETE /api/v1/tracks/[id] processing.\",\n        \"Executes batch deletion of all PlaylistTrack junction records referencing the soft-deleted track ID.\",\n        \"Re-indexes remaining PlaylistTrack positions (position = position - 1 for position > deletedTrackPosition) per affected playlist.\",\n        \"Decrements trackCount metric on all affected Playlist records by 1.\",\n        \"Decrements trackCount metric on the track owner's ArtistProfile record by 1.\",\n        \"Invalidates cache tags for affected playlists and artist catalog listings.\",\n        \"Integration tests in tests/services/playlist-cascade.test.ts assert PlaylistTrack purge, position re-indexing without gaps, and accurate trackCount decrements on Playlist and ArtistProfile.\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 50,\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"STORY-track-009\"\n      ],\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"STORY-track-011\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement Asynchronous Storage Media Asset Purging Pipeline for Archived Tracks\",\n      \"description\": \"Implement the TrackMediaPurgeJob background task queue worker that permanently deletes physical audio (audioStorageKey) and cover image (coverStorageKey) files from object storage (S3/R2) following track soft-deletion.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"Triggered asynchronously via task queue event emitted after successful Track soft-deletion.\",\n        \"TrackMediaPurgeJob retrieves audioStorageKey and coverStorageKey for the archived track ID.\",\n        \"Invokes StorageProvider.deleteFile() for both the audio binary asset and cover image asset.\",\n        \"Handles missing keys or storage API failures with exponential backoff retries and structured error logging.\",\n        \"Preserves database record in archived state for analytical history while confirming storage objects are purged.\",\n        \"Unit and integration tests in tests/jobs/track-media-purge.test.ts verify worker invocation, target storage key deletion calls, and error retry handling.\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 51,\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"STORY-track-009\",\n        \"STORY-storage-001\"\n      ],\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"STORY-track-012\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement Frontend Artist Catalog Management Page and Track Edit Form\",\n      \"description\": \"Build the artist catalog management interface and interactive track metadata edit modal using Next.js, React Hook Form, and shadcn/ui. Enable artists to view uploaded tracks and edit title, cover artwork URL/file, and genre tag with real-time feedback.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"Renders artist catalog list displaying track artwork, title, genre badge, upload timestamp, play count, and Edit/Delete action controls.\",\n        \"Clicking Edit opens a modal dialog pre-populated with current title, cover image, and genre dropdown matching system taxonomy.\",\n        \"Validates form inputs displaying inline errors for title (1-100 characters) and invalid cover image URLs or files over 5MB.\",\n        \"Submitting form calls PATCH /api/v1/tracks/[id] and updates catalog list UI state and Next.js revalidated data upon 200 OK success response.\",\n        \"Modal and form elements satisfy WCAG 2.1 AA accessibility guidelines (keyboard focus trapping, ARIA dialog labels, visible focus rings).\",\n        \"Playwright spec in e2e/tests/artist-catalog-edit.spec.ts verifies opening edit modal, modifying title and genre, submitting valid form, and asserting updated UI listing.\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 52,\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"STORY-track-007\",\n        \"STORY-profile-007\"\n      ],\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"STORY-track-013\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement Frontend Track Deletion Dialog and Active Player Queue Synchronization\",\n      \"description\": \"Build the track deletion confirmation dialog in the artist catalog dashboard and implement real-time player bar and queue state synchronization when an actively playing or queued track is edited or soft-deleted.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"Clicking Delete in artist catalog opens a confirmation dialog warning that soft-archiving removes the track from user playlists.\",\n        \"Confirming deletion calls DELETE /api/v1/tracks/[id] and removes track row from artist catalog UI upon 200 OK.\",\n        \"If active playing track metadata is modified by the artist, persistent player bar updates title and artwork seamlessly without interrupting playback.\",\n        \"If actively playing/queued track is deleted, browser audio buffer plays to completion, player marks queue item unavailable, displays toast notification ('Track removed by artist'), and advances to next valid queue item.\",\n        \"Confirmation dialog and player alerts comply with WCAG 2.1 AA keyboard accessibility and screen reader announcement standards (aria-live).\",\n        \"Playwright spec in e2e/tests/artist-catalog-delete.spec.ts covers deletion dialog confirmation, catalog item removal, and player toast notification trigger on active track deletion.\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 53,\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"STORY-track-009\",\n        \"STORY-track-012\"\n      ],\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"STORY-player-001\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement Audio Player React Context and Session Persistence Provider\",\n      \"description\": \"Create the AudioPlayerProvider React context wrapper in app/layout.tsx above child page routes. The provider maintains global player state, encapsulates a hidden HTML5 audio element, exposes useAudioPlayer(), and persists session metadata to browser sessionStorage under indie_player_session for seamless state restoration on tab reloads.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"AudioPlayerProvider is mounted in app/layout.tsx root layout and exposes useAudioPlayer() context hook to all child page routes.\",\n        \"Player state encapsulates PlaybackStatus ('IDLE', 'LOADING', 'BUFFERING', 'PLAYING', 'PAUSED', 'ERROR'), currentTrack metadata, currentTime, duration, volume, isMuted, repeatMode ('OFF', 'ALL', 'ONE'), and isShuffleActive.\",\n        \"A hidden HTML5 <audio> element is mounted inside AudioPlayerProvider and abstracts native events (timeupdate, ended, waiting, playing, error, stalled) into application state updates.\",\n        \"Active track and queue state are automatically mirrored to sessionStorage under key indie_player_session upon state changes.\",\n        \"On tab reload, the provider restores track metadata and seek timestamp from indie_player_session in a PAUSED state without triggering immediate auto-play.\",\n        \"Unit tests in context/AudioPlayerContext.test.tsx verify state transitions, event subscriptions, and sessionStorage serialization.\",\n        \"Playwright spec in e2e/tests/player-persistence.spec.ts verifies player state remains active across client-side page route navigation.\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 54,\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"STORY-setup-002\",\n        \"STORY-setup-003\"\n      ],\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"STORY-player-002\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement Audio Player Queue State Engine and Shuffling Actions\",\n      \"description\": \"Implement in-memory queue management logic inside AudioPlayerProvider with a hard cap of 500 items. Provides queue manipulation actions including immediate track play with context queue, insertion next, appending to queue end, drag-and-drop reordering, Fisher-Yates shuffle toggle preserving original queue order, and repeat mode management.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"Queue state maintains originalQueue, activeQueue, historyStack, and currentIndex with an enforced maximum limit of 500 items.\",\n        \"playTrackImmediately(track, contextQueue) loads target track, updates activeQueue with context queue if supplied, and sets currentIndex.\",\n        \"insertQueueNext(tracks) appends target tracks directly after currentIndex, while addToQueueEnd(tracks) appends items to the end of activeQueue.\",\n        \"playNextTrack() and playPreviousTrack() correctly navigate activeQueue, handling historyStack pops and repeatMode ('OFF', 'ALL', 'ONE') boundaries.\",\n        \"toggleShuffle() creates a randomized permutation of activeQueue items following currentIndex using the Fisher-Yates algorithm while preserving originalQueue.\",\n        \"Disabling shuffle restores activeQueue to originalQueue while matching currentIndex to the currently active track.\",\n        \"Unit tests in utils/queueEngine.test.ts cover queue insertion, reordering, Fisher-Yates shuffle integrity, and repeat mode boundary conditions.\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 55,\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"STORY-player-001\"\n      ],\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"STORY-player-003\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement Persistent Bottom Audio Player Bar UI Component\",\n      \"description\": \"Build the persistent AudioPlayerBar component fixed to the bottom of the viewport in root layout. Features track cover art and title display, play/pause controls, seek progress slider with visual drag jitter protection, volume slider with logarithmic scaling, mute toggle, and retry handling for stream buffering and network errors.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"AudioPlayerBar component is rendered in app/layout.tsx and styled with fixed bottom positioning using dark-mode design system tokens.\",\n        \"Displays current track cover art, track title, artist name, current seek position, and total duration formatted as MM:SS.\",\n        \"Seek slider supports click-jump and drag scrubbing, pausing timeupdate event updates during drag to eliminate thumb jitter.\",\n        \"Volume slider maps normalized float (0.0-1.0) to audio element volume using logarithmic formula V_effective = V^2.5 and persists setting under localStorage key indie_player_volume.\",\n        \"Toggling mute silences output while preserving previous volume level for restoration upon unmute.\",\n        \"Stream errors trigger up to 3 retry attempts with exponential backoff (1s, 2s, 4s) before showing a non-blocking toast error in player UI.\",\n        \"Component unit tests in components/player/AudioPlayerBar.test.tsx verify play/pause toggles, volume scaling, seek events, and error UI states.\",\n        \"Playwright spec in e2e/tests/player-bar.spec.ts verifies audio playback controls and volume persistence.\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 56,\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"STORY-player-001\"\n      ],\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"STORY-player-004\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement Slide-Out Queue Drawer Overlay Component\",\n      \"description\": \"Build the slide-out queue overlay panel component toggled from the player bar. Displays the current track, upcoming queued tracks, track durations, drag-and-drop item reordering controls, track removal buttons, and a clear queue action.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"Slide-out queue panel opens via a queue toggle button on AudioPlayerBar with accessible overlay backdrop.\",\n        \"Renders currently playing track highlight alongside the scrollable list of activeQueue items.\",\n        \"Supports drag-and-drop repositioning of queued tracks, calling reorderQueue(startIndex, endIndex) without interrupting active playback.\",\n        \"Individual tracks can be removed via a delete button, triggering removeFromQueue(index).\",\n        \"Clear queue button empties activeQueue up to the current playing track and updates queue drawer state.\",\n        \"Component unit tests in components/player/QueueDrawer.test.tsx verify render list, drag reordering triggers, and clear queue button actions.\",\n        \"Playwright spec in e2e/tests/queue-drawer.spec.ts verifies opening the drawer, reordering items, and removing tracks.\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 57,\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"STORY-player-002\",\n        \"STORY-player-003\"\n      ],\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"effort\": \"small\",\n      \"model\": \"haiku\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"STORY-player-005\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement MediaSession API Integration and Platform Keyboard Shortcuts\",\n      \"description\": \"Integrate the browser navigator.MediaSession API to sync playback state and metadata with OS hardware media controls. Implement platform-wide keyboard hotkeys for play/pause, seek, volume, and track skip, along with WCAG 2.1 AA ARIA attributes and screen reader announcements.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"navigator.mediaSession.metadata is updated on track load with title, artist, album name, and cover artwork variants (96x96, 256x256, 512x512).\",\n        \"Binds MediaSession action handlers for play, pause, previoustrack, nexttrack, seekto, and stop.\",\n        \"Global keyboard hotkeys are active platform-wide: Space/K (Play/Pause), M (Mute), Left/Right Arrows (5s seek), J/L (10s seek), Shift+N/P (Next/Prev track).\",\n        \"Keyboard shortcuts are automatically suppressed when user focus resides inside input fields, textareas, or select dropdowns.\",\n        \"Seek and volume sliders include role='slider', aria-valuenow, aria-valuemin, aria-valuemax, aria-valuetext, and 2px high-contrast focus rings.\",\n        \"An aria-live='polite' screen reader region announces track changes ('Now playing: Track Title by Artist Name').\",\n        \"Unit tests in hooks/useMediaSession.test.tsx and hooks/usePlayerHotkeys.test.tsx cover event binding and input suppression logic.\",\n        \"Playwright spec in e2e/tests/player-accessibility.spec.ts verifies hotkey execution and ARIA slider attributes.\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 58,\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"STORY-player-001\",\n        \"STORY-player-003\"\n      ],\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"effort\": \"medium\",\n      \"model\": \"deepseek\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"STORY-player-006\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement Unauthenticated Guest Playback and Auth Prompt Interceptor\",\n      \"description\": \"Ensure unauthenticated guest users can stream public tracks and public playlists without login tokens. Add an authentication modal trigger interceptor when guest users click interactive social buttons (Like, Follow, Save) on the persistent player bar UI without halting active playback.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"Guest users can stream public tracks using signed GET media delivery URLs without requiring auth tokens.\",\n        \"Guest player bar maintains session queue and volume preferences in sessionStorage and localStorage.\",\n        \"Clicking 'Like Track', 'Follow Artist', or 'Save to Playlist' from the player bar while unauthenticated triggers the auth prompt modal.\",\n        \"Audio playback continues uninterrupted in background while the auth prompt modal is visible.\",\n        \"Unit tests in components/player/GuestAuthInterceptor.test.tsx verify social action interception for guests.\",\n        \"Playwright spec in e2e/tests/guest-playback.spec.ts verifies unauthenticated track playback and auth modal trigger.\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 59,\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"STORY-player-001\",\n        \"STORY-player-003\"\n      ],\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"effort\": \"small\",\n      \"model\": \"haiku\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"STORY-listen-001\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement Play Session Initialization API Endpoint\",\n      \"description\": \"Create the POST /api/v1/tracks/:id/play-session API endpoint that issues a time-bound HMAC-SHA256 signed playbackToken containing trackId, sessionId, issuedAt, and requiredThresholdSeconds calculated as min(30s, 0.5 * duration).\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"Endpoint POST /api/v1/tracks/:id/play-session accepts trackId parameter and returns 200 OK with PlaySessionResponse.\",\n        \"Calculates requiredThresholdSeconds as min(30, 0.5 * Track.duration) based on database Track record.\",","numLines":1310,"startLine":1,"totalLines":2473,"truncatedByTokenCap":true}}}
